\c 8
\s1 How Majestic Is Your Name!
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb According to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Gittith.|הַגִּתִּ֗ית\rb*\f + \fr 8:1 \fqa Gittith\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in \ref Psalms 81|81\ref* and 84.\f* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our Lord,|אֲדֹנֵ֗ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb how|מָֽה־\rb* \rb majestic|אַדִּ֣יר\rb* \rb is Your name|שִׁ֭מְךָ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth!|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb You|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb have set|תְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb Your glory|ה֝וֹדְךָ֗\rb*
\q2 \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the heavens.|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb From the mouths|מִפִּ֤י\rb* \rb of children|עֽוֹלְלִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb and infants|וְֽיֹנְקִים֮\rb*
\q2 \rb You have ordained|יִסַּ֪דְתָּ֫\rb* \rb praise|עֹ֥ז\rb*\f + \fr 8:2 \ft Literally \fqa You have ordained strength\ft ; LXX \fqa You have prepared praise\ft ; cited in \ref Matthew 21:16|MAT 21:16\ref*\f*
\q1 \rb on account of|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb Your adversaries,|צוֹרְרֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb to silence|לְהַשְׁבִּ֥ית\rb* \rb the enemy|א֝וֹיֵ֗ב\rb* \rb and avenger.|וּמִתְנַקֵּֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I behold|אֶרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb Your heavens,|שָׁ֭מֶיךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of Your fingers,|אֶצְבְּעֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb the moon|יָרֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb and the stars,|וְ֝כוֹכָבִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have set in place—|כּוֹנָֽנְתָּה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is man|אֱנ֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You are mindful of him,|תִזְכְּרֶ֑נּוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb or the son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָ֝דָ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You care for him?|תִפְקְדֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You made him a little lower|וַתְּחַסְּרֵ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |מְּ֭עַט\rb* \rb than the angels;|מֵאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 8:5 \ft Or \fqa than God \ft or \fqa than the heavenly beings\ft ; see also LXX.\f*
\q2 \rb You crowned him|תְּעַטְּרֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb with glory|וְכָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb and honor.|וְהָדָ֣ר\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb You made him ruler|תַּ֭מְשִׁילֵהוּ\rb* \rb of the works|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of Your hands;|יָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb You have placed|שַׁ֣תָּה\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֝ל\rb* \rb under|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb his feet:|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*\f + \fr 8:6 \ft Cited \ref in 1|1\ref* Corinthians 15:27 and Hebrews 2:6–8\f*
\q1 \v 7 \rb all|כֻּלָּ֑ם\rb* \rb sheep|צֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and oxen,|וַאֲלָפִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and even|וְ֝גַ֗ם\rb* \rb the beasts|בַּהֲמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the field,|שָׂדָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb the birds|צִפּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the air|שָׁ֭מַיִם\rb* \rb and the fish|וּדְגֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sea,|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb all that swim|עֹ֝בֵ֗ר\rb* \rb the paths|אָרְח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the seas.|יַמִּֽים׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our Lord,|אֲדֹנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb how|מָֽה־\rb* \rb majestic|אַדִּ֥יר\rb* \rb is Your name|שִׁ֝מְךָ֗\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth!|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\c 9
\s1 I Will Give Thanks to the LORD
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַ֭מְנַצֵּחַ\rb* \rb To the tune of “The Death of the Son.”|לַבֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft \ref Psalms 9|9\ref* and 10 together follow an acrostic pattern, each stanza beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet. In the LXX they form one psalm.\f*
\q1 \rb I will give thanks|אוֹדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb my heart;|לִבִּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb I will recount|אֲ֝סַפְּרָ֗ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Your wonders.|נִפְלְאוֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will be glad|אֶשְׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb and rejoice|וְאֶעֶלְצָ֣ה\rb* \rb in You;|בָ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I will sing praise|אֲזַמְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Your name,|שִׁמְךָ֣\rb* \rb O Most High.|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb When my enemies|אוֹיְבַ֥י\rb* \rb retreat,|בְּשׁוּב־\rb*\rb |אָח֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb they stumble|יִכָּשְׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb and perish|וְ֝יֹאבְד֗וּ\rb* \rb before You.|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You have upheld|עָ֭שִׂיתָ\rb* \rb my just|מִשְׁפָּטִ֣י\rb* \rb cause;|וְדִינִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb You sit|יָשַׁ֥בְתָּ\rb* \rb on Your throne|לְ֝כִסֵּ֗א\rb* \rb judging|שׁוֹפֵ֥ט\rb* \rb righteously.|צֶֽדֶק׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You have rebuked|גָּעַ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb the nations;|ג֭וֹיִם\rb*
\q2 \rb You have destroyed|אִבַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb the wicked;|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb*
\q2 \rb You have erased|מָ֝חִ֗יתָ\rb* \rb their name|שְׁמָ֥ם\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever.|וָעֶֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb The enemy|הָֽאוֹיֵ֨ב׀\rb*\rb |תַּ֥מּוּ\rb* \rb has come to eternal|לָ֫נֶ֥צַח\rb* \rb ruin,|חֳרָב֗וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and You have uprooted|נָתַ֑שְׁתָּ\rb* \rb their cities;|וְעָרִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb the very memory|זִכְרָ֣ם\rb* \rb of them|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb has vanished.|אָבַ֖ד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb But the LORD|וַֽ֭יהוָה\rb* \rb abides|יֵשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb forever;|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb He has established|כּוֹנֵ֖ן\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְאֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb for judgment.|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֣ט\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb He|וְה֗וּא\rb* \rb judges|יִשְׁפֹּֽט־\rb* \rb the world|תֵּבֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with justice;|בְּצֶ֑דֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb He governs|יָדִ֥ין\rb* \rb the people|לְ֝אֻמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb with equity.|בְּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb is|וִ֘יהִ֤י\rb* \rb a refuge|מִשְׂגָּ֣ב\rb* \rb for the oppressed,|לַדָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb a stronghold|מִ֝שְׂגָּ֗ב\rb* \rb in times|לְעִתּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of trouble.|בַּצָּרָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Those who know|יוֹדְעֵ֣י\rb* \rb Your name|שְׁמֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb trust|וְיִבְטְח֣וּ\rb* \rb in You,|בְ֭ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb You, O LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb forsaken|עָזַ֖בְתָּ\rb* \rb those who seek You.|דֹרְשֶׁ֣יךָ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Sing praises|זַמְּר֗וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַ֭יהוָה\rb* \rb who dwells|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Zion;|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb proclaim|הַגִּ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb His deeds|עֲלִֽילוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb among the nations.|בָ֝עַמִּ֗ים\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Avenger|דֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of bloodshed|דָּ֭מִים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb remembers;|זָכָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb He does not ignore|שָׁ֝כַ֗ח\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the cry|צַעֲקַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the afflicted.|עֲנִיִּים׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Be merciful to me,|חָֽנְנֵ֬נִי\rb* \rb O LORD;|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb see|רְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb how my enemies|מִשֹּׂנְאָ֑י\rb* \rb afflict me!|עָ֭נְיִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Lift me up|מְ֝רוֹמְמִ֗י\rb* \rb from the gates|מִשַּׁ֥עֲרֵי\rb* \rb of death,|מָֽוֶת׃\rb*
\q2 \v 14 \rb that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb I may declare|אֲסַפְּרָ֗ה\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb Your praises—|תְּהִלָּ֫תֶ֥יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb that within the gates|בְּשַֽׁעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb Zion|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb I may rejoice|אָ֝גִ֗ילָה\rb* \rb in Your salvation.|בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb The nations|ג֭וֹיִם\rb* \rb have fallen|טָבְע֣וּ\rb* \rb into a pit|בְּשַׁ֣חַת\rb* \rb of their making;|עָשׂ֑וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb their feet|רַגְלָֽם׃\rb* \rb are caught|נִלְכְּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the net|בְּרֶֽשֶׁת־\rb*\rb |ז֥וּ\rb* \rb they have hidden.|טָ֝מָ֗נוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb is known|נ֤וֹדַ֨ע׀\rb* \rb by the justice|מִשְׁפָּ֪ט\rb* \rb He brings;|עָ֫שָׂ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the wicked|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb are ensnared|נוֹקֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb by the work|בְּפֹ֣עַל\rb* \rb of their hands.|כַּ֭פָּיו\rb*
\qr \rb Higgaion|הִגָּי֥וֹן\rb* \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \fqa Higgaion Selah \ft or \fqa quiet interlude \ft is probably a musical or liturgical term.\f*
\q1 \v 17 \rb The wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb will return|יָשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Sheol—|לִשְׁא֑וֹלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|גּ֝וֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb who forget|שְׁכֵחֵ֥י\rb* \rb God.|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the needy|אֶבְי֑וֹן\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb always|לָ֭נֶצַח\rb* \rb be forgotten;|יִשָּׁכַ֣ח\rb*
\q2 \rb nor the hope|תִּקְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the oppressed|עֲנָוִים\rb* \rb forever|לָעַֽד׃\rb* \rb dashed.|תֹּאבַ֥ד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Rise up,|קוּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb do not let|אַל־\rb* \rb man|אֱנ֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb prevail;|יָעֹ֣ז\rb*
\q2 \rb let the nations|ג֝וֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb be judged|יִשָּׁפְט֥וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb Your presence.|פָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb Lay|שִׁ֘יתָ֤ה\rb* \rb terror|מוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb upon them, O LORD;|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb*
\q2 \rb let the nations|גוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb know|יֵדְע֥וּ\rb* \rb they|לָ֫הֶ֥ם\rb* \rb are but men.|אֱנ֖וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |הֵ֣מָּה\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶּֽלָה׃\rb*
\c 10
\s1 The Perils of the Pilgrim
\q1 \v 1 \rb Why,|לָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb do You stand|תַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb far off?|בְּרָח֑וֹק\rb*
\q2 \rb Why do You hide|תַּ֝עְלִ֗ים\rb* \rb in times|לְעִתּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of trouble?|בַּצָּרָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb In pride|בְּגַאֲוַ֣ת\rb* \rb the wicked|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb pursue|יִדְלַ֣ק\rb* \rb the needy;|עָנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb let them be caught|יִתָּפְשׂ֓וּ׀\rb* \rb in the schemes|בִּמְזִמּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |ז֣וּ\rb* \rb they devise.|חָשָֽׁבוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the wicked man|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb boasts|הִלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the cravings|תַּאֲוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of his heart;|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb he blesses|בֵּ֝רֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb the greedy|וּבֹצֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb and reviles|נִ֘אֵ֥ץ׀\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb In his pride|כְּגֹ֣בַהּ\rb*\rb |אַ֭פּוֹ\rb* \rb the wicked man|רָשָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb does not|בַּל־\rb* \rb seek Him;|יִדְרֹ֑שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb in all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his schemes|מְזִמּוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb God.|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb He is secure|יָ֘חִ֤ילוּ\rb* \rb in his ways|דַרְכּוֹ\rb* \rb at all times;|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֗ת\rb*
\q2 \rb Your lofty|מָר֣וֹם\rb* \rb judgments|מִ֭שְׁפָּטֶיךָ\rb* \rb are far from him;|מִנֶּגְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb he sneers|יָפִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb at|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his foes.|צ֝וֹרְרָ֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb He says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to himself,|בְּ֭לִבּוֹ\rb* \rb “I will not|בַּל־\rb* \rb be moved;|אֶמּ֑וֹט\rb*
\q2 \rb from age|לְדֹ֥ר\rb* \rb to age|וָ֝דֹ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I am free|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of distress.”|בְרָֽע׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb His mouth|פִּ֣יהוּ\rb* \rb is full of|מָ֭לֵא\rb* \rb cursing,|אָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb deceit,|וּמִרְמ֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 10:7 \ft LXX \fqa bitterness\ft ; cited in \ref Romans 3:14|ROM 3:14\ref*\f* \rb and violence;|וָתֹ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb trouble|עָמָ֥ל\rb* \rb and malice|וָאָֽוֶן׃\rb* \rb are under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb his tongue.|לְ֝שׁוֹנ֗וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb He lies|יֵשֵׁ֤ב׀\rb* \rb in wait|בְּמַאְרַ֬ב\rb* \rb near the villages;|חֲצֵרִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in ambush|בַּֽ֭מִּסְתָּרִים\rb* \rb he slays|יַהֲרֹ֣ג\rb* \rb the innocent;|נָקִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb his eyes|עֵ֝ינָ֗יו\rb* \rb watch in stealth|יִצְפֹּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb for the helpless.|לְֽחֵלְכָ֥ה\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb He lies in wait|יֶאֱרֹ֬ב\rb*\rb |בַּמִּסְתָּ֨ר׀\rb* \rb like a lion|כְּאַרְיֵ֬ה\rb* \rb in a thicket;|בְסֻכֹּ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb he lurks|יֶ֭אֱרֹב\rb* \rb to seize|לַחֲט֣וֹף\rb* \rb the oppressed;|עָנִ֑י\rb*
