\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֤חַ׀\rb* \rb Of David|לְדָ֫וִ֥ד\rb* \rb the servant|לְעֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb sang|דִּבֶּ֨ר׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דִּ֭בְרֵי\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֤וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֘ה\rb* \rb had delivered|הִֽצִּיל־\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his enemies|אֹ֝יְבָ֗יו\rb* \rb and from the hand|וּמִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of Saul.|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb He said:|וַיֹּאמַ֡ר\rb*
