\q1 \rb The heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb* \rb declare|מְֽסַפְּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb the glory|כְּבֽוֹד־\rb* \rb of God;|אֵ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb the skies|הָרָקִֽיעַ׃\rb* \rb proclaim|מַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb the work|וּֽמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of His hands.|יָ֝דָ֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb after day|לְ֭יוֹם\rb* \rb they pour forth|יַבִּ֣יעַֽ\rb* \rb speech;|אֹ֑מֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb night|וְלַ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb after night|לְּ֝לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb they reveal|יְחַוֶּה־\rb* \rb knowledge.|דָּֽעַת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Without|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb speech|אֹ֭מֶר\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb language,|דְּבָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb without a sound|קוֹלָֽם׃\rb*\rb |בְּ֝לִ֗י\rb* \rb to be heard,|נִשְׁמָ֥ע\rb*\f + \fr 19:3 \ft Or \fqa There is no speech or language where their voice is not heard\f*
\q1 \v 4 \rb their voice|קַוָּ֗ם\rb*\f + \fr 19:4 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa their measuring line\f* \rb has gone out|יָ֘צָ֤א\rb* \rb into all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth,|הָאָ֨רֶץ׀\rb*
\q2 \rb their words|מִלֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to the ends|וּבִקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the world.|תֵ֭בֵל\rb*\f + \fr 19:4 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 10:18|ROM 10:18\ref*\f*
\b 
\q1 \rb In the heavens|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb He has pitched|שָֽׂם־\rb*
