\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֓ה׀\rb* \rb blesses|יְבָרֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb with peace.|בַשָּׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\c 30
\s1 You Turned My Mourning into Dancing
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm.|מִזְמ֡וֹר\rb* \rb A song|שִׁיר־\rb* \rb for the dedication|חֲנֻכַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the temple.|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb Of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \rb I will exalt You,|אֲרוֹמִמְךָ֣\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You have lifted me up|דִלִּיתָ֑נִי\rb*
\q1 \rb and have not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb allowed my foes|אֹיְבַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb to rejoice|שִׂמַּ֖חְתָּ\rb* \rb over me.|לִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God,|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb* \rb I cried to You|אֵ֝לֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb for help,|שִׁוַּ֥עְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb and You healed me.|וַתִּרְפָּאֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb O LORD,|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb You pulled me|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb up|הֶֽעֱלִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Sheol;|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb You spared me|חִ֝יִּיתַ֗נִי\rb* \rb from descending|מִיּוֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb into the Pit.|בֽוֹר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Sing|זַמְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb O you His saints,|חֲסִידָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and praise|וְ֝הוֹד֗וּ\rb* \rb His holy|קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb name.|לְזֵ֣כֶר\rb*\f + \fr 30:4 \ft Or \fqa and praise the memorial of His holiness\ft ; see \ref Exodus 3:15|EXO 3:15\ref*.\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb His anger|בְּאַפּוֹ֮\rb* \rb is fleeting,|רֶ֨גַע׀\rb*
\q2 \rb but His favor|בִּרְצ֫וֹנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb lasts a lifetime.|חַיִּ֪ים\rb*
\q1 \rb Weeping|בֶּ֗כִי\rb* \rb may stay|יָלִ֥ין\rb* \rb the night,|בָּ֭עֶרֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb but joy comes|רִנָּֽה׃\rb* \rb in the morning.|וְלַבֹּ֥קֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb In prosperity|בְשַׁלְוִ֑י\rb* \rb I|וַ֭אֲנִי\rb* \rb said,|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb “I will never|בַּל־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb be shaken.”|אֶמּ֥וֹט\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb O LORD,|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb You favored me;|בִּרְצוֹנְךָ֮\rb*
\q2 \rb You made|הֶעֱמַ֪דְתָּה\rb* \rb my mountain|לְֽהַרְרִ֫י\rb* \rb stand strong.|עֹ֥ז\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb When You hid|הִסְתַּ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb Your face,|פָנֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb I was|הָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb dismayed.|נִבְהָֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb To You,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb I called,|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb I begged|אֶתְחַנָּֽן׃\rb* \rb my Lord for mercy:|אֲ֝דֹנָ֗י\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb gain is there|בֶּ֥צַע\rb* \rb in my bloodshed,|בְּדָמִי֮\rb*\f + \fr 30:9 \ft Or \fqa in my destruction\f*
\q2 \rb in my descent|בְּרִדְתִּ֪י\rb* \rb to|אֶ֫ל־\rb* \rb the Pit?|שָׁ֥חַת\rb*\f + \fr 30:9 \ft Or \fqa to corruption\f*
\q1 \rb Will the dust|עָפָ֑ר\rb* \rb praise You?|הֲיוֹדְךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb Will it proclaim|הֲיַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb Your faithfulness?|אֲמִתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Hear me,|שְׁמַע־\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and have mercy;|וְחָנֵּ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb O LORD,|יְ֝הוָה\rb* \rb be|הֱ‍ֽיֵה־\rb* \rb my helper.”|עֹזֵ֥ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb You turned|הָפַ֣כְתָּ\rb* \rb my mourning|מִסְפְּדִי֮\rb* \rb into dancing;|לְמָח֪וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb You peeled off|פִּתַּ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb my sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֑י\rb* \rb and clothed me|וַֽתְּאַזְּרֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb with joy,|שִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb that my heart|לְמַ֤עַן׀\rb* \rb may sing|יְזַמֶּרְךָ֣\rb* \rb Your praises|כָ֭בוֹד\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be silent.|יִדֹּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God,|אֱ֝לֹהַ֗י\rb* \rb I will give thanks|אוֹדֶֽךָּ׃\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb*
\c 31
\s1 Into Your Hands I Commit My Spirit
\r \ref Luke 23:44–49|LUK 23:44-49\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \rb In You,|בְּךָ֖\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb I have taken refuge;|חָ֭סִיתִי\rb*
\q2 \rb let me never|אַל־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb be put to shame;|אֵב֣וֹשָׁה\rb*
\q2 \rb save me|פַלְּטֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb by Your righteousness.|בְּצִדְקָתְךָ֥\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Incline|הַטֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Your ear|אָזְנְךָ֮\rb* \rb to me;|אֵלַ֨י׀\rb*
\q2 \rb come quickly|מְהֵרָ֪ה\rb* \rb to my rescue.|הַצִּ֫ילֵ֥נִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Be|הֱיֵ֤ה\rb* \rb my|לִ֨י׀\rb* \rb rock|לְֽצוּר־\rb* \rb of refuge,|מָ֭עוֹז\rb*
\q2 \rb the stronghold|לְבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |מְצוּד֗וֹת\rb* \rb of my deliverance.|לְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb are my rock|סַלְעִ֣י\rb* \rb and my fortress;|וּמְצוּדָתִ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb lead me|תַּֽנְחֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb and guide me|וּֽתְנַהֲלֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb for the sake of|וּלְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb Your name.|שִׁ֝מְךָ֗\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb You free me|תּוֹצִיאֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb from the net|מֵרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |ז֭וּ\rb* \rb laid out|טָ֣מְנוּ\rb* \rb for me,|לִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַ֝תָּה\rb* \rb are my refuge.|מָֽעוּזִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Into Your hands|בְּיָדְךָ֮\rb* \rb I commit|אַפְקִ֪יד\rb* \rb my spirit;|ר֫וּחִ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 31:5 \ft Cited in \ref Luke 23:46|LUK 23:46\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb You have redeemed me,|פָּדִ֖יתָה\rb*\rb |אוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb of truth.|אֱמֶֽת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb I hate|שָׂנֵ֗אתִי\rb*\f + \fr 31:6 \ft MT; one Hebrew manuscript, LXX, and Syriac \fqa You hate\f* \rb those who cling|הַשֹּׁמְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to worthless idols,|הַבְלֵי־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑וְא\rb*
\q2 \rb but in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb I|וַ֝אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb trust.|בָּטָֽחְתִּי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb I will be glad|אָגִ֥ילָה\rb* \rb and rejoice|וְאֶשְׂמְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb in Your loving devotion,|בְּחַ֫סְדֶּ֥ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have seen|רָ֭אִיתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my affliction;|עָנְיִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb You have known|יָ֝דַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb the anguish|בְּצָר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of my soul.|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb You have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb delivered me|הִ֭סְגַּרְתַּנִי\rb* \rb to|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb the enemy;|אוֹיֵ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb You have set|הֶֽעֱמַ֖דְתָּ\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָֽי׃\rb* \rb in the open.|בַמֶּרְחָ֣ב\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Be merciful to me,|חָנֵּ֥נִי\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָה֮\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I am in distress;|צַ֫ר־\rb*
\q1 \rb my eyes|עֵינִ֗י\rb* \rb fail|עָשְׁשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb from sorrow,|בְכַ֥עַס\rb*
\q2 \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb and body as well.|וּבִטְנִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb my life|חַיַּי֮\rb* \rb is consumed|כָל֪וּ\rb* \rb with grief|בְיָג֡וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and my years|וּשְׁנוֹתַ֪י\rb* \rb with groaning;|בַּאֲנָ֫חָ֥ה\rb*
\q1 \rb my iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנִ֣י\rb* \rb has drained|כָּשַׁ֣ל\rb* \rb my strength,|כֹחִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and my bones|וַעֲצָמַ֥י\rb* \rb are wasting away.|עָשֵֽׁשׁוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Among all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb my enemies|צֹרְרַ֨י\rb* \rb I am|הָיִ֪יתִי\rb* \rb a disgrace,|חֶרְפָּ֡ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and among my neighbors|וְלִשֲׁכֵנַ֨י׀\rb* \rb even more.|מְאֹד֮\rb*
\q1 \rb I am dreaded|וּפַ֪חַד\rb* \rb by my friends—|לִֽמְיֻדָּ֫עָ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb they flee|נָדְד֥וּ\rb* \rb when they see|רֹאַ֥י\rb* \rb me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb on the street.|בַּח֑וּץ\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb I am forgotten|נִ֭שְׁכַּחְתִּי\rb* \rb like a dead man,|כְּמֵ֣ת\rb* \rb out of mind.|מִלֵּ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb I am|הָ֝יִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb like a broken|אֹבֵֽד׃\rb* \rb vessel.|כִּכְלִ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I hear|שָׁמַ֨עְתִּי׀\rb* \rb the slander|דִּבַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of many;|רַבִּים֮\rb*
\q2 \rb there is terror|מָג֪וֹר\rb* \rb on every side.|מִסָּ֫בִ֥יב\rb*
\q1 \rb They conspire|בְּהִוָּסְדָ֣ם\rb*\rb |יַ֣חַד\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and plot|זָמָֽמוּ׃\rb* \rb to take|לָקַ֖חַת\rb* \rb my life.|נַפְשִׁ֣י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֤י׀\rb* \rb trust|בָטַ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb in You,|עָלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I say,|אָ֝מַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb “You|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are my God.”|אֱלֹהַ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb My times|עִתֹּתָ֑י\rb* \rb are in Your hands;|בְּיָדְךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb deliver me|הַצִּ֘ילֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb from|מִיַּד־\rb* \rb my enemies|א֝וֹיְבַ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb and from those who pursue me.|וּמֵרֹדְפָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Make Your face|פָ֭נֶיךָ\rb* \rb shine|הָאִ֣ירָה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Your servant;|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb save me|ה֖וֹשִׁיעֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb by Your loving devotion.|בְחַסְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb O LORD,|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb let me not|אַל־\rb* \rb be ashamed,|אֵ֭בוֹשָׁה\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have called on You.|קְרָאתִ֑יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Let the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb be put to shame;|יֵבֹ֥שׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb let them lie silent|יִדְּמ֥וּ\rb* \rb in Sheol.|לִשְׁאֽוֹל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb May lying|שָׁ֥קֶר\rb* \rb lips|שִׂפְתֵ֫י\rb* \rb be silenced—|תֵּ֥אָלַ֗מְנָה\rb*
\q2 \rb lips that speak|הַדֹּבְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb with arrogance|עָתָ֗ק\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the righteous,|צַדִּ֥יק\rb*
\q2 \rb full of pride|בְּגַאֲוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and contempt.|וָבֽוּז׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb How|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb great|רַֽב־\rb* \rb is Your goodness|טוּבְךָ֮\rb*
\q2 \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You have laid up|צָפַ֪נְתָּ\rb* \rb for those who fear You,|לִּֽירֵ֫אֶ֥יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb which You have bestowed|פָּ֭עַלְתָּ\rb* \rb before|נֶ֝֗גֶד\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of men|אָדָם׃\rb*
\q2 \rb on those who take refuge|לַחֹסִ֣ים\rb* \rb in You!|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb You hide them|תַּסְתִּירֵ֤ם׀\rb* \rb in the secret place|בְּסֵ֥תֶר\rb* \rb of Your presence|פָּנֶיךָ֮\rb*
\q2 \rb from the schemes|מֵֽרֻכְסֵ֫י\rb* \rb of men.|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*
\q1 \rb You conceal them|תִּצְפְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb in Your shelter|בְּסֻכָּ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb from accusing|מֵרִ֥יב\rb* \rb tongues.|לְשֹׁנֽוֹת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb be the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He has shown|הִפְלִ֘יא\rb* \rb me|לִ֝֗י\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֥וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb in a city|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb under siege.|מָצֽוֹר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb In my alarm|בְחָפְזִ֗י\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֤י׀\rb* \rb said,|אָ֘מַ֤רְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb “I am cut off|נִגְרַזְתִּי֮\rb* \rb from|מִנֶּ֪גֶד\rb* \rb Your sight!”|עֵ֫ינֶ֥יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb But|אָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb You heard|שָׁ֭מַעְתָּ\rb* \rb my plea|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb for mercy|תַּחֲנוּנַ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb when I called to You|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb for help.|בְּשַׁוְּעִ֥י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb Love|אֶֽהֱב֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb His saints.|חֲסִ֫ידָ֥יו\rb*
\q2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb preserves|נֹצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the faithful,|אֱ֭מוּנִים\rb*
\q2 \rb but fully|עַל־\rb*\rb |יֶ֝֗תֶר\rb* \rb repays|וּמְשַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb the arrogant.|עֹשֵׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |גַאֲוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 24 \rb Be strong|חִ֭זְקוּ\rb* \rb and courageous,|וְיַאֲמֵ֣ץ\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you who hope|הַ֝מְיַחֲלִ֗ים\rb* \rb in the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\c 32
\s1 The Joy of Forgiveness
\r \ref Romans 4:1–12|ROM 4:1-12\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb Of David.|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb A Maskil.|מַ֫שְׂכִּ֥יל\rb*\f + \fr 32:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f*
\q1 \rb Blessed is he|אַשְׁרֵ֥י\rb* \rb whose transgressions|פֶּ֗שַׁע\rb* \rb are forgiven,|נְֽשׂוּי־\rb*
\q2 \rb whose sins|חֲטָאָֽה׃\rb* \rb are covered.|כְּס֣וּי\rb*\f + \fr 32:1 \ft LXX \fqa Blessed is he whose lawless acts are forgiven, whose sins are covered\ft ; cited in \ref Romans 4:7|ROM 4:7\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Blessed|אַ֥שְֽׁרֵי\rb* \rb is the man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb whose iniquity|עָוֺ֑ן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb count|יַחְשֹׁ֬ב\rb* \rb against him,|ל֣וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 32:2 \ft LXX \fqa Blessed is the man whose sin the LORD does not count against him\ft ; cited in \ref Romans 4:8|ROM 4:8\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb in whose spirit|בְּרוּח֣וֹ\rb* \rb there is no|וְאֵ֖ין\rb* \rb deceit.|רְמִיָּה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I kept silent,|הֶ֭חֱרַשְׁתִּי\rb* \rb my bones|עֲצָמָ֑י\rb* \rb became brittle|בָּל֣וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb from my groaning|בְּ֝שַׁאֲגָתִ֗י\rb* \rb all day long.|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֤י׀\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַיְלָה֮\rb*
\q2 \rb Your hand|יָ֫דֶ֥ךָ\rb* \rb was heavy|תִּכְבַּ֥ד\rb* \rb upon me;|עָלַ֗י\rb*
\q1 \rb my strength|לְשַׁדִּ֑י\rb* \rb was drained|נֶהְפַּ֥ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 32:4 \ft Or \fqa my vitality was turned\f*
\q2 \rb as in the summer|קַ֣יִץ\rb* \rb heat.|בְּחַרְבֹ֖נֵי\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Then I acknowledged|אוֹדִ֪יעֲךָ֡\rb* \rb my sin to You|חַטָּאתִ֨י\rb*
\q2 \rb and did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb hide|כִסִּ֗יתִי\rb* \rb my iniquity.|וַעֲוֺ֘נִ֤י\rb*
\q1 \rb I said,|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb “I will confess|אוֹדֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb my transgressions|פְ֭שָׁעַי\rb* \rb to the LORD,”|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and You|וְאַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb forgave|נָ֘שָׂ֤אתָ\rb* \rb the guilt|עֲוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb of my sin.|חַטָּאתִ֣י\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |זֹ֡את\rb* \rb let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the godly|חָסִ֨יד׀\rb* \rb pray|יִתְפַּלֵּ֬ל\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶיךָ֮\rb*
\q2 \rb while|לְעֵ֪ת\rb* \rb You may be found.|מְ֫צֹ֥א\rb*
\q1 \rb Surely|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb when great|רַבִּ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֝לָ֗יו\rb* \rb waters|לְ֭שֵׁטֶף\rb* \rb rise,|מַ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb they will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb come near.|יַגִּֽיעוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb are my hiding place.|סֵ֥תֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb You protect me|תִּ֫צְּרֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb from trouble;|מִצַּ֪ר\rb*
\q2 \rb You surround me|תְּס֖וֹבְבֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb with songs|רָנֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of deliverance.|פַלֵּ֑ט\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb I will instruct you|אַשְׂכִּֽילְךָ֨׀\rb* \rb and teach|וְֽאוֹרְךָ֗\rb* \rb you the way|בְּדֶֽרֶךְ־\rb*\rb |ז֥וּ\rb* \rb you should go;|תֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I will give you counsel|אִֽיעֲצָ֖ה\rb* \rb and watch|עֵינִֽי׃\rb* \rb over you.|עָלֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be|תִּֽהְי֤וּ׀\rb* \rb like the horse|כְּס֥וּס\rb* \rb or mule,|כְּפֶרֶד֮\rb*
\q2 \rb which have no|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb understanding;|הָ֫בִ֥ין\rb*
\q1 \rb they must be controlled|לִבְל֑וֹם\rb* \rb with bit|בְּמֶֽתֶג־\rb* \rb and bridle|וָרֶ֣סֶן\rb*\rb |עֶדְי֣וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb to make them|בַּ֝֗ל\rb* \rb come|קְרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Many|רַבִּ֥ים\rb* \rb are the sorrows|מַכְאוֹבִ֗ים\rb* \rb of the wicked,|לָרָ֫שָׁ֥ע\rb*
\q2 \rb but loving devotion|חֶ֝֗סֶד\rb* \rb surrounds him|יְסוֹבְבֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb who trusts|וְהַבּוֹטֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb in the LORD.|בַּיהוָ֑ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Be glad|שִׂמְח֬וּ\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and rejoice,|וְ֭גִילוּ\rb* \rb O righteous ones;|צַדִּיקִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb shout for joy,|וְ֝הַרְנִ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you upright|יִשְׁרֵי־\rb* \rb in heart.|לֵֽב׃\rb*
\c 33
\s1 Praise to the Creator
\r \ref Psalm 148:1–14|PSA 148:1-14\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Rejoice|רַנְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb in the LORD,|בַּֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb O righteous ones;|צַ֭דִּיקִים\rb*
\q2 \rb it is fitting|נָאוָ֥ה\rb* \rb for the upright|לַ֝יְשָׁרִ֗ים\rb* \rb to praise Him.|תְהִלָּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Praise|הוֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb with the harp;|בְּכִנּ֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb make music|זַמְּרוּ־\rb* \rb to Him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb with ten strings.|עָ֝שׂ֗וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥בֶל\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Sing|שִֽׁירוּ־\rb* \rb to Him|ל֭וֹ\rb* \rb a new|חָדָ֑שׁ\rb* \rb song;|שִׁ֣יר\rb*
\q2 \rb play|נַ֝גֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb skillfully|הֵיטִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb with a shout of joy.|בִּתְרוּעָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is upright,|יָשָׁ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb His work|מַ֝עֲשֵׂ֗הוּ\rb* \rb is trustworthy.|בֶּאֱמוּנָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb The LORD loves|אֹ֭הֵב\rb* \rb righteousness|צְדָקָ֣ה\rb* \rb and justice;|וּמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*
\q2 \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb is full of|מָלְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb His|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb* \rb loving devotion.|חֶ֥סֶד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb By the word|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb were made,|נַעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the stars|צְבָאָֽם׃\rb* \rb by the breath|וּבְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of His mouth.|פִּ֝֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb He piles up|כֹּנֵ֣ס\rb*\rb |כַּ֭נֵּד\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sea;|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb He puts|נֹתֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the depths|תְּהוֹמֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb into storehouses.|בְּאֹצָר֣וֹת\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb fear|יִֽירְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb the LORD;|מֵ֭יְהוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the world|תֵבֵֽל׃\rb* \rb revere Him.|יָ֝ג֗וּרוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb spoke,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb and it came to be;|וַיֶּ֑הִי\rb*
\q2 \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb commanded,|צִ֝וָּ֗ה\rb* \rb and it stood firm.|וַֽיַּעֲמֹֽד׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb The LORD|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb frustrates|הֵפִ֥יר\rb* \rb the plans|עֲצַת־\rb* \rb of the nations;|גּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb He thwarts|הֵ֝נִ֗יא\rb* \rb the devices|מַחְשְׁב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the peoples.|עַמִּֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb The counsel|עֲצַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb stands forever,|תַּעֲמֹ֑ד\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb the purposes|מַחְשְׁב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of His heart|לִ֝בּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb to all generations.|לְדֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |וָדֹֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb Blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֣י\rb* \rb is the nation|הַ֭גּוֹי\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb is the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the people|הָעָ֓ם׀\rb* \rb He has chosen|בָּחַ֖ר\rb* \rb as His inheritance!|לְנַחֲלָ֣ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb looks down|הִבִּ֣יט\rb* \rb from heaven;|מִ֭שָּׁמַיִם\rb*
\q2 \rb He sees|רָ֝אָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men.|הָאָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb From His dwelling|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb place|מִֽמְּכוֹן־\rb* \rb He gazes|הִשְׁגִּ֑יחַ\rb*
\q2 \rb on|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who inhabit|שִׁבְתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb He shapes|הַיֹּצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the hearts|לִבָּ֑ם\rb* \rb of each;|יַ֣חַד\rb*
\q2 \rb He considers|הַ֝מֵּבִ֗ין\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their works.|מַעֲשֵׂיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb No|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb king|הַ֭מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb is saved|נוֹשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb by his vast|בְּרָב־\rb* \rb army;|חָ֑יִל\rb*
\q2 \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb warrior|גִּ֝בּ֗וֹר\rb* \rb is delivered|יִנָּצֵ֥ל\rb* \rb by his great|בְּרָב־\rb* \rb strength.|כֹּֽחַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb A horse|הַ֭סּוּס\rb* \rb is a vain hope|שֶׁ֣קֶר\rb* \rb for salvation;|לִתְשׁוּעָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb even its great|וּבְרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb strength|חֵ֝יל֗וֹ\rb* \rb cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb save.|יְמַלֵּֽט׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb are on|אֶל־\rb* \rb those who fear Him,|יְרֵאָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb on those whose hope|לַֽמְיַחֲלִ֥ים\rb* \rb is in His loving devotion|לְחַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb to deliver|לְהַצִּ֣יל\rb* \rb them|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb from death|מִמָּ֣וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb and keep them alive|וּ֝לְחַיּוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb in famine.|בָּרָעָֽב׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Our soul|נַ֭פְשֵׁנוּ\rb* \rb waits|חִכְּתָ֣ה\rb* \rb for the LORD;|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb He|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is our help|עֶזְרֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and our shield.|וּמָגִנֵּ֣נוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb our hearts|לִבֵּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb rejoice|יִשְׂמַ֣ח\rb* \rb in Him,|ב֭וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb we trust|בָטָֽחְנוּ׃\rb* \rb in His holy|קָדְשׁ֣וֹ\rb* \rb name.|בְשֵׁ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb May Your loving devotion|חַסְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb rest|יְהִֽי־\rb* \rb on us,|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb as|כַּ֝אֲשֶׁ֗ר\rb* \rb we put our hope|יִחַ֥לְנוּ\rb* \rb in You.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\c 34
\s1 Taste and See That the LORD Is Good
\r \ref 1 Samuel 21:8–15|1SA 21:8-15\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb Of David,|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb when he pretended|בְּשַׁנּוֹת֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to be insane|טַ֭עְמוֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abimelech,|אֲבִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 34:1 \fqa Abimelech \ft is another name for \fqa Achish\ft ; \ref see 1|1\ref* Samuel 21–29 and 1 Kings 2:39.\f* \rb so that the king drove him|וַֽ֝יְגָרֲשֵׁ֗הוּ\rb* \rb away.|וַיֵּלַֽךְ׃\rb*\f + \fr 34:1 \ft This psalm is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*
\q1 \rb I will bless|אֲבָרֲכָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb at all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb times;|עֵ֑ת\rb*
\q2 \rb His praise|תְּֽהִלָּת֥וֹ\rb* \rb will always|תָּ֝מִ֗יד\rb* \rb be on my lips.|בְּפִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb My soul|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb boasts|תִּתְהַלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb in the LORD;|בַּ֭יהוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb let the oppressed|עֲנָוִ֣ים\rb* \rb hear|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb and rejoice.|וְיִשְׂמָֽחוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Magnify|גַּדְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb with me;|אִתִּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb let us exalt|וּנְרוֹמְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb His name|שְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb together.|יַחְדָּֽו׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb I sought|דָּרַ֣שְׁתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and He answered me;|וְעָנָ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb He delivered me|הִצִּילָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb my fears.|מְ֝גוּרוֹתַ֗י\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Those who look|הִבִּ֣יטוּ\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֣יו\rb* \rb are radiant with joy;|וְנָהָ֑רוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb their faces|וּ֝פְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb shall never|אַל־\rb* \rb be ashamed.|יֶחְפָּֽרוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb This|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb man called out,|קָ֭רָא\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb heard him;|שָׁמֵ֑עַ\rb*
\q2 \rb He saved him|הוֹשִׁיעֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb from all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb his troubles.|צָ֝רוֹתָ֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb The angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֓ה\rb* \rb encamps|חֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb around|סָ֘בִ֤יב\rb* \rb those who fear Him,|לִֽירֵאָ֗יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and he delivers them.|וַֽיְחַלְּצֵֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Taste|טַעֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb and see|וּ֭רְאוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is good;|ט֣וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb blessed|אַֽשְׁרֵ֥י\rb* \rb is the man|הַ֝גֶּ֗בֶר\rb* \rb who takes refuge|יֶחֱסֶה־\rb* \rb in Him!|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*
