\q2 \rb who delights|הֶ֝חָפֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb in His servant’s|עַבְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb well-being.”|שְׁל֣וֹם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb Then my tongue|וּ֭לְשׁוֹנִי\rb* \rb will proclaim|תֶּהְגֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb Your righteousness|צִדְקֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your praises|תְּהִלָּתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long.|הַ֝יּוֹם\rb*
\c 36
\s1 The Transgression of the Wicked
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֬חַ׀\rb* \rb A Psalm of David,|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb* \rb the servant|לְעֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֬ה\rb*
\q1 \rb An oracle|נְאֻֽם־\rb* \rb is in|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb regarding the transgression|פֶּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb of the wicked man:|לָ֭רָשָׁע\rb*
\q1 \rb There is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb fear|פַּ֥חַד\rb* \rb of God|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb before|לְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb his eyes.|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*\f + \fr 36:1 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 3:18|ROM 3:18\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his eyes|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb are too full of conceit|הֶחֱלִ֣יק\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb to detect|לִמְצֹ֖א\rb* \rb or hate|לִשְׂנֹֽא׃\rb* \rb his own sin.|עֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb The words|דִּבְרֵי־\rb* \rb of his mouth|פִ֭יו\rb* \rb are wicked|אָ֣וֶן\rb* \rb and deceitful;|וּמִרְמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb he has ceased|חָדַ֖ל\rb* \rb to be wise|לְהַשְׂכִּ֣יל\rb* \rb and well-doing.|לְהֵיטִֽיב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Even on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִשְׁכָּ֫ב֥וֹ\rb* \rb he plots|יַחְשֹׁ֗ב\rb* \rb wickedness;|אָ֤וֶן׀\rb*
\q2 \rb he sets himself|יִ֭תְיַצֵּב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a path|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb that is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb good;|ט֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb he fails|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to reject|יִמְאָֽס׃\rb* \rb evil.|רָ֝֗ע\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Your loving devotion,|חַסְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb reaches to the heavens,|בְּהַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb Your faithfulness|אֱ֝מֽוּנָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the clouds.|שְׁחָקִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Your righteousness|צִדְקָֽתְךָ֨׀\rb* \rb is like the highest|אֵ֗ל\rb* \rb mountains;|כְּֽהַרְרֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb Your judgments are|מִ֭שְׁפָּטֶךָ\rb* \rb like the deepest sea.|תְּה֣וֹם\rb*\rb |רַבָּ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb You preserve|תוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb* \rb man|אָ֤דָֽם־\rb* \rb and beast.|וּבְהֵמָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb precious|יָּקָ֥ר\rb* \rb is Your loving devotion,|חַסְדְּךָ֗\rb* \rb O God,|אֱלֹ֫הִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb that the children|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb take refuge|יֶחֱסָיֽוּן׃\rb*
\q2 \rb in the shadow|בְּצֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of Your wings!|כְּ֝נָפֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb They feast on|יִ֭רְוְיֻן\rb* \rb the abundance|מִדֶּ֣שֶׁן\rb* \rb of Your house,|בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and You give them drink|תַשְׁקֵֽם׃\rb* \rb from Your river|וְנַ֖חַל\rb* \rb of delights.|עֲדָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb with You|עִ֭מְּךָ\rb* \rb is the fountain|מְק֣וֹר\rb* \rb of life;|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in Your light|בְּ֝אוֹרְךָ֗\rb* \rb we see|נִרְאֶה־\rb* \rb light.|אֽוֹר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Extend|מְשֹׁ֣ךְ\rb* \rb Your loving devotion|חַ֭סְדְּךָ\rb* \rb to those who know You,|לְיֹדְעֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your righteousness|וְ֝צִדְקָֽתְךָ֗\rb* \rb to the upright|לְיִשְׁרֵי־\rb* \rb in heart.|לֵֽב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Let not|אַל־\rb* \rb the foot|רֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb of the proud|גַּאֲוָ֑ה\rb* \rb come against me,|תְּ֭בוֹאֵנִי\rb*
\q2 \rb nor the hand|וְיַד־\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb drive me|תְּנִדֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb away.|אַל־\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb There|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the evildoers|פֹּ֣עֲלֵי\rb*\rb |אָ֑וֶן\rb* \rb lie fallen,|נָ֭פְלוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb thrown down|דֹּ֝ח֗וּ\rb* \rb and unable|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |יָ֥כְלוּ\rb* \rb to rise.|קֽוּם׃\rb*
\c 37
\s1 Delight Yourself in the LORD
\r \ref 1 Kings 2:1–9|1KI 2:1-9\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb Of David.|לְדָוִ֨ד׀\rb*\f + \fr 37:1 \ft This psalm is an acrostic poem, each stanza beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*
\q1 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fret over|תִּתְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb those who do evil;|בַּמְּרֵעִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb envy|תְּ֝קַנֵּ֗א\rb* \rb those who do|בְּעֹשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb wrong.|עַוְלָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they wither|יִמָּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָ֣ה\rb* \rb like grass|כֶ֭חָצִיר\rb*
\q2 \rb and wilt|יִבּוֹלֽוּן׃\rb* \rb like tender|וּכְיֶ֥רֶק\rb* \rb plants.|דֶּ֝֗שֶׁא\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Trust|בְּטַ֣ח\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּֽ֭יהוָה\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb good;|ט֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb dwell|שְׁכָן־\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֝֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and cultivate|וּרְעֵ֥ה\rb* \rb faithfulness.|אֱמוּנָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Delight yourself|וְהִתְעַנַּ֥ג\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and He will give|וְיִֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לְ֝ךָ֗\rb* \rb the desires|מִשְׁאֲלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of your heart.|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Commit|גּ֣וֹל\rb* \rb your way|דַּרְכֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb trust|וּבְטַ֥ח\rb* \rb in Him,|עָ֝לָ֗יו\rb* \rb and He|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb will do it.|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb He will bring forth|וְהוֹצִ֣יא\rb* \rb your righteousness|צִדְקֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb like the dawn,|כָא֣וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb your justice|וּ֝מִשְׁפָּטֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb like the noonday sun.|כַּֽצָּהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb Be still|דּ֤וֹם׀\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָה֮\rb*
\q2 \rb and wait patiently|וְהִתְח֪וֹלֵ֫ל\rb* \rb for Him;|ל֥וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fret|תִּ֭תְחַר\rb* \rb when men prosper|בְּמַצְלִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb in their ways,|דַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb when they|בְּ֝אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb carry out|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb wicked schemes.|מְזִמּֽוֹת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Refrain|הֶ֣רֶף\rb* \rb from anger|מֵ֭אַף\rb* \rb and abandon|וַעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb wrath;|חֵמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fret—|תִּ֝תְחַ֗ר\rb* \rb it can only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb bring harm.|לְהָרֵֽעַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the evildoers|מְ֭רֵעִים\rb* \rb will be cut off,|יִכָּרֵת֑וּן\rb*
\q2 \rb but those who hope|וְקֹוֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the LORD|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb will inherit|יִֽירְשׁוּ־\rb* \rb the land.|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Yet a little while,|וְע֣וֹד\rb*\rb |מְ֭עַט\rb* \rb and the wicked|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb will be no more;|וְאֵ֣ין\rb*
\q2 \rb though you look|וְהִתְבּוֹנַ֖נְתָּ\rb* \rb for them,|עַל־\rb*\rb |מְקוֹמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb they will not be found.|וְאֵינֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb But the meek|וַעֲנָוִ֥ים\rb* \rb will inherit|יִֽירְשׁוּ־\rb* \rb the land|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*\f + \fr 37:11 \ft Or \fqa the earth\ft ; see \ref Matthew 5:5|MAT 5:5\ref*.\f*
\q2 \rb and delight|וְ֝הִתְעַנְּג֗וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb abundant|רֹ֥ב\rb* \rb prosperity.|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb The wicked|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb scheme|זֹמֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against the righteous|לַצַּדִּ֑יק\rb*
\q2 \rb and gnash|וְחֹרֵ֖ק\rb* \rb their teeth|שִׁנָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb at them,|עָלָ֣יו\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb but the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb laughs,|יִשְׂחַק־\rb*
\q2 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb seeing|רָ֝אָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their day|יוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is coming.|יָבֹ֥א\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The wicked|רְשָׁעִים֮\rb* \rb have drawn|פָּֽתְח֣וּ\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֤רֶב׀\rb*
\q2 \rb and bent|וְדָרְכ֪וּ\rb* \rb the bow|קַ֫שְׁתָּ֥ם\rb*
\q1 \rb to bring down|לְ֭הַפִּיל\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb and needy,|וְאֶבְי֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb to slay|לִ֝טְב֗וֹחַ\rb* \rb those whose ways|דָֽרֶךְ׃\rb* \rb are upright.|יִשְׁרֵי־\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb But their swords|חַ֭רְבָּם\rb* \rb will pierce|תָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb their own hearts,|בְלִבָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and their bows|וְ֝קַשְּׁתוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb will be broken.|תִּשָּׁבַֽרְנָה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Better is|טוֹב־\rb* \rb the little|מְ֭עַט\rb* \rb of the righteous|לַצַּדִּ֑יק\rb*
\q2 \rb than the abundance|מֵ֝הֲמ֗וֹן\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb who are wicked.|רְשָׁעִ֥ים\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the arms|זְרוֹע֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֭שָׁעִים\rb* \rb will be broken,|תִּשָּׁבַ֑רְנָה\rb*
\q2 \rb but the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb upholds|וְסוֹמֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb the righteous.|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the blameless,|תְמִימִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and their inheritance|וְ֝נַחֲלָתָ֗ם\rb* \rb will last forever.|תִּהְיֶֽה׃\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb In the time|בְּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of evil|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb they will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be ashamed,|יֵ֭בֹשׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and in the days|וּבִימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of famine|רְעָב֣וֹן\rb* \rb they will be satisfied.|יִשְׂבָּֽעוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb But|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb and enemies|וְאֹיְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb will perish|יֹאבֵ֗דוּ\rb* \rb like the glory|כִּיקַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the fields.|כָּרִ֑ים\rb*
\q1 \rb They will vanish;|כָּל֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb like smoke|בֶעָשָׁ֣ן\rb* \rb they will fade away.|כָּֽלוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb The wicked|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb borrow|לֹוֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb repay,|יְשַׁלֵּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb but the righteous|וְ֝צַדִּ֗יק\rb* \rb are gracious|חוֹנֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and giving.|וְנוֹתֵֽן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb Surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb those He blesses|מְ֭בֹרָכָיו\rb* \rb will inherit|יִ֣ירְשׁוּ\rb* \rb the land,|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb but the cursed|וּ֝מְקֻלָּלָ֗יו\rb* \rb will be destroyed.|יִכָּרֵֽתוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb The steps|מִֽצְעֲדֵי־\rb* \rb of a man|גֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb are ordered|כּוֹנָ֗נוּ\rb* \rb by the LORD|מֵ֭יְהוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb who takes delight|יֶחְפָּֽץ׃\rb* \rb in his journey.|וְדַרְכּ֥וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 24 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he falls,|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb he will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be overwhelmed,|יוּטָ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb* \rb is holding|סוֹמֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb his hand.|יָדֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 37:24 \ft Or \fqa upholds him with His hand\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb I once was|הָיִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb young|נַ֤עַר׀\rb* \rb and now|גַּם־\rb* \rb am old,|זָ֫קַ֥נְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb yet never|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb have I seen|רָ֭אִיתִי\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb abandoned|נֶעֱזָ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb or their children|וְ֝זַרְע֗וֹ\rb* \rb begging|מְבַקֶּשׁ־\rb* \rb for bread.|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 26 \rb They are|כָּל־\rb* \rb ever|הַ֭יּוֹם\rb* \rb generous|חוֹנֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and quick to lend,|וּמַלְוֶ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and their children|וְ֝זַרְע֗וֹ\rb* \rb are a blessing.|לִבְרָכָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb Turn away|ס֣וּר\rb* \rb from evil|מֵ֭רָע\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb good,|ט֗וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb so that you will abide|וּשְׁכֹ֥ן\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 28 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb* \rb loves|אֹ֘הֵ֤ב\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb*
\q2 \rb and will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb forsake|יַעֲזֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His saints.|חֲ֭סִידָיו\rb*
\q1 \rb They are preserved|נִשְׁמָ֑רוּ\rb* \rb forever,|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb but the offspring|וְזֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be cut off.|נִכְרָֽת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 29 \rb The righteous|צַדִּיקִ֥ים\rb* \rb will inherit|יִֽירְשׁוּ־\rb* \rb the land|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and dwell|וְיִשְׁכְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb forever.|לָעַ֣ד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb The mouth|פִּֽי־\rb* \rb of the righteous man|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb utters|יֶהְגֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb wisdom,|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and his tongue|וּ֝לְשׁוֹנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb speaks|תְּדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb justice.|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*
\q1 \v 31 \rb The law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֣יו\rb* \rb is in his heart;|בְּלִבּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb his steps|אֲשֻׁרָיו׃\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb falter.|תִמְעַ֣ד\rb*
\b 
