\q2 \rb and He will raise you up|וִֽ֭ירוֹמִמְךָ\rb* \rb to inherit|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb the land.|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb When the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb are cut off,|בְּהִכָּרֵ֖ת\rb*
\q2 \rb you will see it.|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 35 \rb I have seen|רָ֭אִיתִי\rb* \rb a wicked,|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb ruthless man|עָרִ֑יץ\rb*
\q2 \rb flourishing|רַעֲנָֽן׃\rb* \rb like a well-rooted|וּ֝מִתְעָרֶ֗ה\rb* \rb native tree,|כְּאֶזְרָ֥ח\rb*
\q1 \v 36 \rb yet he passed away|וַ֭יַּֽעֲבֹר\rb* \rb and was no more;|אֵינֶ֑נּוּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb though I searched,|וָֽ֝אֲבַקְשֵׁ֗הוּ\rb* \rb he could not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be found.|נִמְצָֽא׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 37 \rb Consider|שְׁמָר־\rb* \rb the blameless|תָּ֭ם\rb* \rb and observe|וּרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb the upright,|יָשָׁ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb posterity awaits|אַחֲרִ֖ית\rb* \rb the man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of peace.|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*\f + \fr 37:37 \ft Or \fqa for there is a future for the man of peace\f*
