\q2 \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb they take refuge|חָ֥סוּ\rb* \rb in Him.|בֽוֹ׃\rb*
\c 38
\s1 Do Not Rebuke Me in Your Anger
\r \ref Psalm 6:1–10|PSA 6:1-10\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb of David,|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb for remembrance.|לְהַזְכִּֽיר׃\rb*
\q1 \rb O LORD,|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb rebuke me|תוֹכִיחֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb in Your anger|בְּקֶצְפְּךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb or discipline me|תְיַסְּרֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb in Your wrath.|וּֽבַחֲמָתְךָ֥\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Your arrows|חִ֭צֶּיךָ\rb* \rb have pierced me deeply,|נִ֣חֲתוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your hand|יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb has pressed down|וַתִּנְחַ֖ת\rb* \rb on me.|עָלַ֣י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb There is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb soundness|מְתֹ֣ם\rb* \rb in my body|בִּ֭בְשָׂרִי\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Your anger;|זַעְמֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb there is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb rest|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb in my bones|בַּ֝עֲצָמַ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb my sin.|חַטָּאתִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb my iniquities|עֲ֭וֺנֹתַי\rb* \rb have overwhelmed|עָבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb me;|רֹאשִׁ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb they are a burden|כְּמַשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb too heavy|כָ֝בֵ֗ד\rb* \rb to bear.|יִכְבְּד֥וּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb My wounds|חַבּוּרֹתָ֑י\rb* \rb are foul|הִבְאִ֣ישׁוּ\rb* \rb and festering|נָ֭מַקּוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִ֝פְּנֵ֗י\rb* \rb my sinful folly.|אִוַּלְתִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb I am bent|נַעֲוֵ֣יתִי\rb* \rb and brought low;|שַׁחֹ֣תִי\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*
\q2 \rb all day long|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַ֝יּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb I go about|הִלָּֽכְתִּי׃\rb* \rb mourning.|קֹדֵ֥ר\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my loins|כְ֭סָלַי\rb* \rb are full of|מָלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb burning pain,|נִקְלֶ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb soundness|מְ֝תֹ֗ם\rb* \rb remains in my body.|בִּבְשָׂרִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb I am numb|נְפוּג֣וֹתִי\rb* \rb and badly|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb crushed;|וְנִדְכֵּ֣יתִי\rb*
\q2 \rb I groan|שָׁ֝אַ֗גְתִּי\rb* \rb in anguish|מִֽנַּהֲמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of heart.|לִבִּֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb O Lord,|אֲ‍ֽדֹנָי\rb* \rb my every|כָל־\rb* \rb desire|תַּאֲוָתִ֑י\rb* \rb is before You;|נֶגְדְּךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb my groaning|וְ֝אַנְחָתִ֗י\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb hidden|נִסְתָּֽרָה׃\rb* \rb from You.|מִמְּךָ֥\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb My heart|לִבִּ֣י\rb* \rb pounds,|סְ֭חַרְחַר\rb* \rb my strength|כֹחִ֑י\rb* \rb fails,|עֲזָבַ֣נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and even|גַּם־\rb*\rb |הֵ֝֗ם\rb* \rb the light|וְֽאוֹר־\rb* \rb of my eyes|עֵינַ֥י\rb* \rb has faded.|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |אִתִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb My beloved|אֹֽהֲבַ֨י׀\rb* \rb and friends|וְרֵעַ֗י\rb* \rb shun|יַעֲמֹ֑דוּ\rb*\rb |מִנֶּ֣גֶד\rb* \rb my disease,|נִגְעִ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and my kinsmen|וּ֝קְרוֹבַ֗י\rb* \rb stand|עָמָֽדוּ׃\rb* \rb at a distance.|מֵרָחֹ֥ק\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb Those who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֬י\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb lay snares;|וַיְנַקְשׁ֤וּ׀\rb*
\q2 \rb those who wish me|וְדֹרְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb harm|רָ֭עָתִי\rb* \rb speak|דִּבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb destruction,|הַוּ֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb plotting|יֶהְגּֽוּ׃\rb* \rb deceit|וּ֝מִרְמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long.|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb But like a deaf man,|כְ֭חֵרֵשׁ\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb hear;|אֶשְׁמָ֑ע\rb*
\q2 \rb and like a mute man,|וּ֝כְאִלֵּ֗ם\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb open|יִפְתַּח־\rb* \rb my mouth.|פִּֽיו׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb I am|וָאֱהִ֗י\rb* \rb like a man|כְּ֭אִישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb hear,|שֹׁמֵ֑עַ\rb*
\q2 \rb whose mouth|בְּ֝פִ֗יו\rb* \rb offers no reply.|תּוֹכָחֽוֹת׃\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֥ין\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb I wait|הוֹחָ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb for You,|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb O LORD;|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb will answer,|תַ֝עֲנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb my God.|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I said,|אָ֭מַרְתִּי\rb* \rb “Let them not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb gloat|יִשְׂמְחוּ־\rb* \rb over me—|לִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb those who taunt|הִגְדִּֽילוּ׃\rb* \rb me|עָלַ֥י\rb* \rb when my foot|רַ֝גְלִ֗י\rb* \rb slips.”|בְּמ֥וֹט\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲ֭נִי\rb* \rb am ready|נָכ֑וֹן\rb* \rb to fall,|לְצֶ֣לַע\rb*
\q2 \rb and my pain|וּמַכְאוֹבִ֖י\rb* \rb is ever|תָמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb with me.|נֶגְדִּ֣י\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Yes,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I confess|אַגִּ֑יד\rb* \rb my iniquity;|עֲוֺנִ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb I am troubled|אֶ֝דְאַ֗ג\rb* \rb by my sin.|מֵֽחַטָּאתִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb Many are my enemies|וְֽ֭אֹיְבַי\rb* \rb without cause,|חַיִּ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 38:19 \ft One DSS manuscript; MT \fqa My enemies are vigorous and strong\f*\rb |עָצֵ֑מוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and many|וְרַבּ֖וּ\rb* \rb hate me|שֹׂנְאַ֣י\rb* \rb without reason.|שָֽׁקֶר׃\rb*\f + \fr 38:19 \ft See \ref John 15:25|JHN 15:25\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 20 \rb Those who repay|וּמְשַׁלְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb my good|טוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb with|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb evil|רָ֭עָה\rb*
\q2 \rb attack me|יִ֝שְׂטְנ֗וּנִי\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb pursuing|רְדוֹפִי\rb* \rb the good.|טֽוֹב׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb forsake me,|תַּֽעַזְבֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb O LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb be not|אַל־\rb* \rb far|תִּרְחַ֥ק\rb* \rb from me,|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb O my God.|אֱ֝לֹהַ֗י\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb Come quickly|ח֥וּשָׁה\rb* \rb to help me,|לְעֶזְרָתִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb O Lord|אֲ֝דֹנָ֗י\rb* \rb my Savior.|תְּשׁוּעָתִֽי׃\rb*
\c 39
\s1 I Will Watch My Ways
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb For Jeduthun.|לִידִיתוּן\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \rb I said,|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb “I will watch|אֶֽשְׁמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb my ways|דְרָכַי֮\rb*
\q2 \rb so that I will not sin|מֵחֲט֪וֹא\rb* \rb with my tongue;|בִלְשׁ֫וֹנִ֥י\rb*
\q1 \rb I will guard|אֶשְׁמְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb my mouth|לְפִ֥י\rb* \rb with a muzzle|מַחְס֑וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb as long as|בְּעֹ֖ד\rb* \rb the wicked|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb are present.”|לְנֶגְדִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb I was speechless|נֶאֱלַ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb and still;|ד֭וּמִיָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb I remained silent,|הֶחֱשֵׁ֣יתִי\rb* \rb even from speaking good,|מִטּ֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb and my sorrow|וּכְאֵבִ֥י\rb* \rb was stirred.|נֶעְכָּֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb My heart|לִבִּ֨י׀\rb* \rb grew hot|חַם־\rb* \rb within me;|בְּקִרְבִּ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb as I mused,|בַּהֲגִיגִ֥י\rb* \rb the fire|אֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb burned.|תִבְעַר־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Then I spoke|דִּ֝בַּ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb with my tongue:|בִּלְשֽׁוֹנִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb “Show me,|הוֹדִ֘יעֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb* \rb my end|קִצִּ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb and the measure|וּמִדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of my days.|יָמַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb Let me know|אֵ֝דְעָ֗ה\rb*\rb |מֶה־\rb* \rb how|מַה־\rb*\rb |הִ֑יא\rb* \rb fleeting|חָדֵ֥ל\rb* \rb my life is.|אָֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You, indeed,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb have made|נָ֘תַ֤תָּה\rb* \rb my days|יָמַ֗י\rb* \rb as handbreadths,|טְפָח֨וֹת׀\rb*
\q2 \rb and my lifetime|וְחֶלְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb as nothing|כְאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb before You.|נֶגְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Truly|אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb each|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb man|אָ֝דָ֗ם\rb* \rb at his best|נִצָּ֥ב\rb*
\q2 \rb exists as but a breath.|הֶ֥בֶל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb every man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb goes about|יִֽתְהַלֶּךְ־\rb* \rb like a phantom;|בְּצֶ֤לֶם׀\rb*
\q2 \rb surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb he bustles|יֶהֱמָי֑וּן\rb* \rb in vain;|הֶ֥בֶל\rb*
\q1 \rb he heaps up riches|יִ֝צְבֹּ֗ר\rb*
\q2 \rb not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb knowing|יֵדַ֥ע\rb* \rb who|מִי־\rb* \rb will haul them away.|אֹסְפָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb And now,|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb for what|מַה־\rb* \rb do I wait?|קִּוִּ֣יתִי\rb*
\q2 \rb My hope is|תּ֝וֹחַלְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb in|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb You.|הִֽיא׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Deliver me|הַצִּילֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb my transgressions;|פְּשָׁעַ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb make me|תְּשִׂימֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb the reproach|חֶרְפַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of fools.|נָ֝בָ֗ל\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb I have become mute;|נֶ֭אֱלַמְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb open|אֶפְתַּח־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb because of what|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have done.|עָשִֽׂיתָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Remove|הָסֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Your scourge|נִגְעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb from me;|מֵעָלַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am perishing|כָלִֽיתִי׃\rb* \rb by the force|מִתִּגְרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Your hand.|יָ֝דְךָ֗\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb You discipline|יִסַּ֬רְתָּ\rb* \rb and correct|בְּֽתוֹכָ֘ח֤וֹת\rb* \rb a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his iniquity,|עָוֺ֨ן׀\rb*
\q2 \rb consuming|וַתֶּ֣מֶס\rb* \rb like a moth|כָּעָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb what he holds dear;|חֲמוּד֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb surely|אַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb each|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb is but a vapor.|הֶ֖בֶל\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb Hear|שִֽׁמְעָ֥ה־\rb* \rb my prayer,|תְפִלָּתִ֨י׀\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֡ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and give ear|הַאֲזִינָה֮\rb* \rb to my cry for help;|וְשַׁוְעָתִ֨י׀\rb*
\q1 \rb do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb be deaf|תֶּ֫חֱרַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb my weeping.|דִּמְעָתִ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am a foreigner|גֵ֣ר\rb* \rb dwelling with You,|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb a stranger|תּ֝וֹשָׁ֗ב\rb* \rb like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb my fathers.|אֲבוֹתָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Turn Your gaze|הָשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb away from me,|מִמֶּ֣נִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb that I may again be cheered|וְאַבְלִ֑יגָה\rb*
\q2 \rb before|בְּטֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb I depart|אֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and am no more.”|וְאֵינֶֽנִּי׃\rb*
\c 40
\s1 I Waited Patiently for the LORD
\r \ref Psalm 70:1–5|PSA 70:1-5\ref*; \ref Hebrews 10:1–18|HEB 10:1-18\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַ֝מְנַצֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִ֥ד\rb*
\q1 \rb I waited patiently for|קַוֺּ֣ה\rb*\rb |קִוִּ֣יתִי\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb He inclined|וַיֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb to me|אֵ֝לַ֗י\rb* \rb and heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb my cry.|שַׁוְעָתִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb He lifted me up|וַיַּעֲלֵ֤נִי׀\rb* \rb from the pit|מִבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of despair,|שָׁאוֹן֮\rb*
