\c 44
\s1 Redeem Us, O God
\r \ref Romans 8:35–39|ROM 8:35-39\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֬חַ\rb* \rb A Maskil|מַשְׂכִּֽיל׃\rb*\f + \fr 44:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f* \rb of the sons|לִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Korah.|קֹ֬רַח\rb*
\q1 \rb We have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְנוּ\rb* \rb with our ears,|בְּאָזְנֵ֬ינוּ\rb* \rb O God;|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb*
\q2 \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb have told|סִפְּרוּ־\rb* \rb us|לָ֑נוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb the work|פֹּ֥עַל\rb* \rb You did|פָּעַ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb in their days,|בִֽ֝ימֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the days|בִּ֣ימֵי\rb* \rb of old.|קֶֽדֶם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb With Your hand|יָדְךָ֡\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb drove out|ה֭וֹרַשְׁתָּ\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and planted our fathers there;|וַתִּטָּעֵ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb You crushed|תָּרַ֥ע\rb* \rb the peoples|לְ֝אֻמִּ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and cast them out.|וַֽתְּשַׁלְּחֵֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb it was not|לֹ֪א\rb* \rb by their sword|בְחַרְבָּ֡ם\rb* \rb that they took|יָ֥רְשׁוּ\rb* \rb the land;|אָ֗רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb their arm|וּזְרוֹעָם֮\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bring them victory.|הוֹשִׁ֪יעָ֫ה\rb*\rb |לָּ֥מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb It was|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by Your right hand,|יְמִֽינְךָ֣\rb*
\q2 \rb Your arm,|וּ֭זְרוֹעֲךָ\rb* \rb and the light|וְא֥וֹר\rb* \rb of Your face,|פָּנֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You favored them.|רְצִיתָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb are my King,|מַלְכִּ֣י\rb* \rb O God,|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb who ordains|צַ֝וֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb victories|יְשׁוּע֥וֹת\rb* \rb for Jacob.|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Through You|בְּ֭ךָ\rb* \rb we repel|נְנַגֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb our foes;|צָרֵ֣ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb through Your name|בְּ֝שִׁמְךָ֗\rb* \rb we trample|נָב֥וּס\rb* \rb our enemies.|קָמֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb trust|אֶבְטָ֑ח\rb* \rb in my bow,|בְקַשְׁתִּ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb nor does my sword|וְ֝חַרְבִּ֗י\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb save me.|תוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי׃\rb*\f + \fr 44:6 \ft Or \fqa give me victory\ft ; similarly in verse 7\f*
\q1 \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You save us|ה֭וֹשַׁעְתָּנוּ\rb* \rb from our enemies;|מִצָּרֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb You put those who hate us|וּמְשַׂנְאֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb to shame.|הֱבִישֽׁוֹתָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb In God|בֵּֽ֭אלֹהִים\rb* \rb we have boasted|הִלַּלְ֣נוּ\rb* \rb all day long,|כָל־\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your name|וְשִׁמְךָ֓׀\rb* \rb we will praise|נוֹדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb But|אַף־\rb* \rb You have rejected|זָ֭נַחְתָּ\rb* \rb and humbled us;|וַתַּכְלִימֵ֑נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb You no longer|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb go forth|תֵ֝צֵ֗א\rb* \rb with our armies.|בְּצִבְאוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb You have made us retreat|תְּשִׁיבֵ֣נוּ\rb*\rb |אָ֭חוֹר\rb* \rb from|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb the foe,|צָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and those who hate us|וּ֝מְשַׂנְאֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb have plundered us.|שָׁ֣סוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb You have given us up|תִּ֭תְּנֵנוּ\rb* \rb as sheep|כְּצֹ֣אן\rb* \rb to be devoured;|מַאֲכָ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb You have scattered us|זֵרִיתָֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb among the nations.|וּ֝בַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb You sell|תִּמְכֹּֽר־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֥\rb* \rb for nothing;|בְלֹא־\rb*
\q2 \rb no|וְלֹ֥א־\rb* \rb profit|ה֑וֹן\rb* \rb do You gain|רִ֝בִּ֗יתָ\rb* \rb from their sale.|בִּמְחִירֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb You have made us|תְּשִׂימֵ֣נוּ\rb* \rb a reproach|חֶ֭רְפָּה\rb* \rb to our neighbors,|לִשְׁכֵנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
