\q1 \v 15 \rb But|אַךְ־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb will redeem|יִפְדֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb my life|נַ֭פְשִׁי\rb* \rb from|מִֽיַּד־\rb* \rb Sheol,|שְׁא֑וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb He will surely take me to Himself.|יִקָּחֵ֣נִי\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּ֭ירָא\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb grows rich,|יַעֲשִׁ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the splendor|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of his house|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb increases.|יִ֝רְבֶּה\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb when he dies,|בְ֭מוֹתוֹ\rb* \rb he will carry|יִקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb nothing away;|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |הַכֹּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb his abundance|כְּבוֹדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb follow him|אַחֲרָ֣יו\rb* \rb down.|יֵרֵ֖ד\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb in his lifetime|בְּחַיָּ֣יו\rb* \rb he blesses|יְבָרֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb his soul—|נַ֭פְשׁוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and men praise|וְ֝יוֹדֻ֗ךָ\rb* \rb you when|כִּי־\rb* \rb you prosper—|תֵיטִ֥יב\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb he will join|תָּ֭בוֹא\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of his fathers,|אֲבוֹתָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb who will never|עַד־\rb*\rb |נֵ֝֗צַח\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb see|יִרְאוּ־\rb* \rb the light of day.|אֽוֹר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb A man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb who has riches|בִּ֭יקָר\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb understanding|יָבִ֑ין\rb*
\q2 \rb is like|נִמְשַׁ֖ל\rb* \rb the beasts|כַּבְּהֵמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb that perish.|נִדְמֽוּ׃\rb*
\c 50
\s1 The Mighty One Calls
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֗וֹר\rb* \rb of Asaph.|לְאָ֫סָ֥ף\rb*
\q1 \rb The Mighty One,|אֵ֤ל׀\rb* \rb God|אֱ‍ֽלֹהִ֡ים\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb speaks|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb and summons|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb from where the sun rises|מִמִּזְרַח־\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb where it sets.|מְבֹאֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֝֗מֶשׁ\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb From Zion,|מִצִּיּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb perfect|מִכְלַל־\rb* \rb in beauty,|יֹ֗פִי\rb*
\q2 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb shines forth.|הוֹפִֽיעַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb approaches|יָ֤בֹ֥א\rb* \rb and will not|וְֽאַל־\rb* \rb be silent!|יֶ֫חֱרַ֥שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb Consuming|תֹּאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb fire|אֵשׁ־\rb* \rb precedes Him,|לְפָנָ֥יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and a tempest|נִשְׂעֲרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb rages around Him.|וּ֝סְבִיבָ֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb He summons|יִקְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb above,|מֵעָ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and the earth,|הָ֝אָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that He may judge|לָדִ֥ין\rb* \rb His people:|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb “Gather|אִסְפוּ־\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb My saints,|חֲסִידָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb who made|כֹּרְתֵ֖י\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִיתִ֣י\rb* \rb with Me|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb by sacrifice.”|זָֽבַח׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb And the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb proclaim|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb His righteousness,|צִדְק֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֓ים׀\rb* \rb Himself|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is Judge.|שֹׁפֵ֖ט\rb*\f + \fr 50:6 \ft Or \fqa He is a God of justice\f*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb “Hear,|שִׁמְעָ֤ה\rb* \rb O My people,|עַמִּ֨י׀\rb* \rb and I will speak,|וַאֲדַבֵּ֗רָה\rb*
\q2 \rb O Israel,|יִ֭שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb and I will testify|וְאָעִ֣ידָה\rb* \rb against you:|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb am God,|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb rebuke|אוֹכִיחֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb you for|עַל־\rb* \rb your sacrifices,|זְ֭בָחֶיךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and your burnt offerings|וְעוֹלֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb are ever|תָמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb before Me.|לְנֶגְדִּ֣י\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb I have no|לֹא־\rb* \rb need|אֶקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb for a bull|פָ֑ר\rb* \rb from your stall|מִבֵּיתְךָ֣\rb*
\q2 \rb or goats|עַתּוּדִֽים׃\rb* \rb from your pens,|מִ֝מִּכְלְאֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb beast|חַיְתוֹ־\rb* \rb of the forest|יָ֑עַר\rb* \rb is Mine—|לִ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb the cattle|בְּ֝הֵמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb on a thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb hills.|בְּהַרְרֵי־\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb I know|יָ֭דַעְתִּי\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb bird|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb in the mountains,|הָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and the creatures|וְזִ֥יז\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂ֝דַ֗י\rb* \rb are Mine.|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I were hungry,|אֶ֭רְעַב\rb* \rb I would not|לֹא־\rb* \rb tell|אֹ֣מַר\rb* \rb you,|לָ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb the world|תֵ֝בֵ֗ל\rb* \rb is Mine,|לִ֥י\rb* \rb and the fullness thereof.|וּמְלֹאָֽהּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Do I eat|הַֽ֭אוֹכַל\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of bulls,|אַבִּירִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb or drink|אֶשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb the blood|וְדַ֖ם\rb* \rb of goats?|עַתּוּדִ֣ים\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb Sacrifice|זְבַ֣ח\rb* \rb a thank offering|תּוֹדָ֑ה\rb* \rb to God,|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and fulfill|וְשַׁלֵּ֖ם\rb* \rb your vows|נְדָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb to the Most High.|לְעֶלְי֣וֹן\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Call upon Me|וּ֭קְרָאֵנִי\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of trouble;|צָרָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I will deliver you,|אֲ֝חַלֶּצְךָ֗\rb* \rb and you will honor Me.”|וּֽתְכַבְּדֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb To the wicked, however,|וְלָ֤רָשָׁ֨ע׀\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb says,|אָ֘מַ֤ר\rb*
\q2 \rb “What right|מַה־\rb* \rb have you|לְּ֭ךָ\rb* \rb to recite|לְסַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקָּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and to bear|וַתִּשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֣י\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb your lips?|פִֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb For you|וְ֭אַתָּה\rb* \rb hate|שָׂנֵ֣אתָ\rb* \rb My instruction|מוּסָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and cast|וַתַּשְׁלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb My words|דְּבָרַ֣י\rb* \rb behind you.|אַחֲרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb you see|רָאִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb a thief,|גַ֭נָּב\rb* \rb you befriend|וַתִּ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb him,|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and throw in your lot|חֶלְקֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb with|וְעִ֖ם\rb* \rb adulterers.|מְנָאֲפִ֣ים\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb You unleash|שָׁלַ֣חְתָּ\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֭יךָ\rb* \rb for evil|בְרָעָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and harness|תַּצְמִ֥יד\rb* \rb your tongue|וּ֝לְשׁוֹנְךָ֗\rb* \rb to deceit.|מִרְמָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb You sit|תֵּ֭שֵׁב\rb* \rb and malign|תְדַבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb your brother;|בְּאָחִ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb you|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb slander|דֹּֽפִי׃\rb* \rb your own mother’s|אִ֝מְּךָ֗\rb* \rb son.|בְּבֶֽן־\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb You have done|עָשִׂ֨יתָ׀\rb* \rb these things,|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb and I kept silent;|וְֽהֶחֱרַ֗שְׁתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb you thought|דִּמִּ֗יתָ\rb* \rb I was|הֱֽיוֹת־\rb*\f + \fr 50:21 \ft Or \fqa you thought the ‘I AM’ was\f* \rb |אֶֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb just like you.|כָמ֑וֹךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb But now I rebuke you|אוֹכִיחֲךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb and accuse you|וְאֶֽעֶרְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb to your face.|לְעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 50:21 \ft Literally \fqa and I set it in order before your eyes\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb consider|בִּֽינוּ־\rb* \rb this,|זֹ֭את\rb* \rb you who forget|שֹׁכְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb God,|אֱל֑וֹהַּ\rb*
\q2 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I tear you to pieces,|אֶ֝טְרֹ֗ף\rb*
\q2 \rb with no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to rescue you:|מַצִּֽיל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 23 \rb He who sacrifices|זֹבֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb a thank offering|תּוֹדָ֗ה\rb* \rb honors Me,|יְֽכַ֫בְּדָ֥נְנִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and to him who rightly orders|וְשָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb his way,|דֶּ֑רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I will show|אַ֝רְאֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb the salvation|בְּיֵ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb of God.”|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\c 51
\s1 Create in Me a Clean Heart, O God
\r \ref 2 Samuel 12:1–12|2SA 12:1-12\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb* \rb When Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb came|בְּֽבוֹא־\rb* \rb to him|אֵ֭לָיו\rb* \rb after|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his adultery|בָּ֝֗א\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba.|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*
\q1 \rb Have mercy on me,|חָנֵּ֣נִי\rb*\f + \fr 51:1 \ft Or \fqa Be gracious to me\f* \rb O God,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb according to Your loving devotion;|כְּחַסְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb according to Your great|כְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb compassion,|רַ֝חֲמֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb blot out|מְחֵ֣ה\rb* \rb my transgressions.|פְשָׁעָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Wash me clean|הַרְבֵּה\rb*\rb |כַּבְּסֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb of my iniquity|מֵעֲוֺנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and cleanse me|טַהֲרֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from my sin.|וּֽמֵחַטָּאתִ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb know|אֵדָ֑ע\rb* \rb my transgressions,|פְ֭שָׁעַי\rb*
\q2 \rb and my sin|וְחַטָּאתִ֖י\rb* \rb is always|תָמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb before me.|נֶגְדִּ֣י\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Against You,|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb You only,|לְבַדְּךָ֨׀\rb* \rb have I sinned|חָטָאתִי֮\rb*
\q2 \rb and done|עָ֫שִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb what is evil|וְהָרַ֥ע\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb so that|לְ֭מַעַן\rb* \rb You may be proved right|תִּצְדַּ֥ק\rb* \rb when You speak|בְּדָבְרֶ֗ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and blameless|תִּזְכֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb when You judge.|בְשָׁפְטֶֽךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 51:4 \ft LXX \fqa and victorious when You judge\ft ; cited in \ref Romans 3:4|ROM 3:4\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Surely|הֵן־\rb* \rb I was brought forth|חוֹלָ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb in iniquity;|בְּעָו֥וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb I was sinful|וּ֝בְחֵ֗טְא\rb* \rb when my mother|אִמִּֽי׃\rb* \rb conceived me.|יֶֽחֱמַ֥תְנִי\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Surely|הֵן־\rb* \rb You desire|חָפַ֣צְתָּ\rb* \rb truth|אֱ֭מֶת\rb* \rb in the inmost being;|בַטֻּח֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb You teach me|תוֹדִיעֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the inmost place.|וּ֝בְסָתֻ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Purify me|תְּחַטְּאֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb with hyssop,|בְאֵז֣וֹב\rb* \rb and I will be clean;|וְאֶטְהָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb wash me,|תְּ֝כַבְּסֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb and I will be whiter|אַלְבִּֽין׃\rb* \rb than snow.|וּמִשֶּׁ֥לֶג\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Let me hear|תַּ֭שְׁמִיעֵנִי\rb* \rb joy|שָׂשׂ֣וֹן\rb* \rb and gladness;|וְשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb let the bones|עֲצָמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb You have crushed|דִּכִּֽיתָ׃\rb* \rb rejoice.|תָּ֝גֵ֗לְנָה\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb Hide|הַסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb Your face|פָּ֭נֶיךָ\rb* \rb from my sins|מֵחֲטָאָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and blot out|מְחֵֽה׃\rb* \rb all|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb my iniquities.|עֲוֺ֖נֹתַ֣י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Create|בְּרָא־\rb* \rb in me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb a clean|טָ֭הוֹר\rb* \rb heart,|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb O God,|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and renew|חַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb a right|נָ֝כ֗וֹן\rb* \rb spirit|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb within me.|בְּקִרְבִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Cast me not away|תַּשְׁלִיכֵ֥נִי\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb from Your presence;|מִלְּפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb take|תִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb Your Holy|קָ֝דְשְׁךָ֗\rb* \rb Spirit|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb from me.|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb Restore|הָשִׁ֣יבָה\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֭י\rb* \rb the joy|שְׂשׂ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Your salvation,|יִשְׁעֶ֑ךָ\rb*
