\c 58
\s1 God Judges the Earth
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb To the tune of|אַל־\rb* \rb “Do Not Destroy.”|תַּשְׁחֵ֗ת\rb* \rb A Miktam|מִכְתָּֽם׃\rb*\f + \fr 58:1 \fqa Miktam\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 16|16\ref* and 56–60.\f* \rb of David.|לְדָוִ֥ד\rb*
\q1 \rb Do you indeed|הַֽאֻמְנָ֗ם\rb* \rb speak|תְּדַבֵּר֑וּן\rb* \rb justly,|צֶ֭דֶק\rb* \rb O rulers?|אֵ֣לֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb Do you judge|תִּ֝שְׁפְּט֗וּ\rb* \rb uprightly,|מֵישָׁרִ֥ים\rb* \rb O sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of men?|אָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb No,|אַף־\rb* \rb in your hearts|בְּלֵב֮\rb* \rb you devise|תִּפְעָ֫ל֥וּן\rb* \rb injustice;|עוֹלֹ֪ת\rb*
\q2 \rb with your hands|יְ֝דֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb you mete out|תְּפַלֵּֽסֽוּן׃\rb* \rb violence|חֲמַ֥ס\rb* \rb on the earth.|בָּאָ֡רֶץ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb The wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb are estranged|זֹ֣רוּ\rb* \rb from the womb;|מֵרָ֑חֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb the liars|דֹּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |כָזָֽב׃\rb* \rb go astray|תָּע֥וּ\rb* \rb from birth.|מִ֝בֶּ֗טֶן\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Their venom|חֲמַת־\rb*\rb |לָ֗מוֹ\rb* \rb is like|כִּדְמ֥וּת\rb* \rb the venom|חֲמַת־\rb* \rb of a snake,|נָחָ֑שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb like|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb a cobra|פֶ֥תֶן\rb* \rb that shuts|חֵ֝רֵ֗שׁ\rb*\rb |יַאְטֵ֥ם\rb* \rb its ears,|אָזְנֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb refusing|לֹא־\rb* \rb to hear|יִ֭שְׁמַע\rb* \rb the tune|לְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the charmer|מְלַחֲשִׁ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb who skillfully|מְחֻכָּֽם׃\rb* \rb weaves his spell.|חוֹבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |חֲבָרִ֣ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb O God,|אֱ‍ֽלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb shatter|הֲרָס־\rb* \rb their teeth|שִׁנֵּ֥ימוֹ\rb* \rb in their mouths;|בְּפִ֑ימוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb tear out|נְתֹ֣ץ׀\rb* \rb the fangs|מַלְתְּע֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the lions.|כְּ֝פִירִ֗ים\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb May they vanish|יִמָּאֲס֣וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb like|כְמוֹ־\rb* \rb water|מַ֭יִם\rb* \rb that runs off;|יִתְהַלְּכוּ־\rb*
\q1 \rb when they draw the bow,|יִדְרֹ֥ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb may their arrows|חִצּוֹ\rb* \rb be blunted.|יִתְמֹלָֽלוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 58:7 \ft Or \fqa when they are trodden down, may they wither like grass\f*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Like|כְּמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb a slug|שַׁ֭בְּלוּל\rb* \rb that dissolves|יַהֲלֹ֑ךְ\rb* \rb in its slime,|תֶּ֣מֶס\rb*
\q2 \rb like a woman’s|אֵ֝֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb stillborn child,|נֵ֥פֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb may they never|בַּל־\rb* \rb see|חָ֥זוּ\rb* \rb the sun.|שָֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Before|בְּטֶ֤רֶם\rb* \rb your pots|סִּֽירֹתֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb can feel|יָבִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb the burning thorns—|אָטָ֑ד\rb*
\q2 \rb whether green|חַ֥י\rb* \rb or|כְּמוֹ־\rb*\rb |כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb dry—|חָ֝ר֗וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb He will sweep them away.|יִשְׂעָרֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb The righteous|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb will rejoice|יִשְׂמַ֣ח\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּי־\rb* \rb they see|חָזָ֣ה\rb* \rb they are avenged;|נָקָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb they will wash|יִ֝רְחַ֗ץ\rb* \rb their feet|פְּעָמָ֥יו\rb*
\q2 \rb in the blood|בְּדַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the wicked.|הָרָשָֽׁע׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Then men|אָ֭דָם\rb* \rb will say,|וְיֹאמַ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb “There is surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb a reward|פְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb for the righteous!|לַצַּדִּ֑יק\rb*
\q2 \rb There is|יֵשׁ־\rb* \rb surely|אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb a God|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb who judges|שֹׁפְטִ֥ים\rb* \rb the earth!”|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\c 59
\s1 Deliver Me from My Enemies
\r \ref 1 Samuel 19:1–24|1SA 19:1-24\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb To the tune of|אַל־\rb* \rb “Do Not Destroy.”|תַּשְׁחֵת֮\rb* \rb A Miktam|מִ֫כְתָּ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 59:1 \fqa Miktam\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 16|16\ref* and 56–60.\f* \rb of David,|לְדָוִ֪ד\rb* \rb when Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb sent|בִּשְׁלֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb men to watch|וַֽיִּשְׁמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David’s house|הַ֝בַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb in order to kill him.|לַהֲמִיתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \rb Deliver me|הַצִּילֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb from my enemies,|מֵאֹיְבַ֥י׀\rb* \rb O my God;|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb protect me|תְּשַׂגְּבֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from those who rise against me.|מִּמִתְקוֹמְמַ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Deliver me|הַ֭צִּילֵנִי\rb* \rb from workers|מִפֹּ֣עֲלֵי\rb* \rb of iniquity,|אָ֑וֶן\rb*\rb |וּֽמֵאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb and save me|הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from men of bloodshed.|דָ֝מִ֗ים\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb See|הִנֵּ֪ה\rb* \rb how they lie in wait|אָֽרְב֡וּ\rb* \rb for me.|לְנַפְשִׁ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb Fierce men|עַזִ֑ים\rb* \rb conspire|יָג֣וּרוּ\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb for no|לֹא־\rb* \rb transgression|פִשְׁעִ֖י\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb sin of my own,|חַטָּאתִ֣י\rb* \rb O LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb For no|בְּֽלִי־\rb* \rb fault of my own,|עָ֭וֺן\rb*
\q2 \rb they move swiftly|יְרוּצ֣וּן\rb* \rb to attack me.|וְיִכּוֹנָ֑נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Arise|ע֖וּרָה\rb* \rb to help me,|לִקְרָאתִ֣י\rb* \rb and take notice.|וּרְאֵה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb |וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb O LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֡וֹת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹ֘הֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*
\q2 \rb rouse Yourself|הָקִ֗יצָה\rb* \rb to punish|לִפְקֹ֥ד\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the nations;|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb show no|אַל־\rb* \rb mercy|תָּחֹ֨ן\rb* \rb to the|כָּל־\rb* \rb wicked|אָ֣וֶן\rb* \rb traitors.|בֹּ֖גְדֵי\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb They return|יָשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb in the evening,|לָ֭עֶרֶב\rb* \rb snarling|יֶהֱמ֥וּ\rb* \rb like dogs|כַכָּ֗לֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb and prowling around|וִיס֥וֹבְבוּ\rb* \rb the city.|עִֽיר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb See what|הִנֵּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb they spew|יַבִּ֘יע֤וּן\rb* \rb from their mouths—|בְּפִיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb sharp words|חֲ֭רָבוֹת\rb* \rb from their lips:|בְּשִׂפְתוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb “For|כִּי־\rb* \rb who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb can hear us?”|שֹׁמֵֽעַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb But You,|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb laugh|תִּשְׂחַק־\rb* \rb at them;|לָ֑מוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb You scoff|תִּ֝לְעַ֗ג\rb* \rb at all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the nations.|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb I will keep watch|אֶשְׁמֹ֑רָה\rb* \rb for You,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O my strength,|עֻ֭זּוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb because You,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb O God,|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb are my fortress.|מִשְׂגַּבִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb My God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of loving devotion|חַסְדּוֹ\rb* \rb will come to meet me;|יְקַדְּמֵ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb God|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb will let me stare down|יַרְאֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb my foes.|בְשֹׁרְרָֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb kill them,|תַּהַרְגֵ֤ם׀\rb*
\q2 \rb or|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb my people|עַמִּ֗י\rb* \rb will forget.|יִשְׁכְּח֬וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb Scatter them|הֲנִיעֵ֣מוֹ\rb* \rb by Your power,|בְ֭חֵילְךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and bring them down,|וְהוֹרִידֵ֑מוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָֽי׃\rb* \rb our shield.|מָֽגִנֵּ֣נוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb By the sins|חַטַּאת־\rb* \rb of their mouths|פִּ֗ימוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the words|דְּֽבַר־\rb* \rb of their lips,|שְׂפָ֫תֵ֥ימוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb let them be trapped|וְיִלָּכְד֥וּ\rb* \rb in their pride,|בִגְאוֹנָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the curses|וּמֵאָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and lies|וּמִכַּ֣חַשׁ\rb* \rb they utter.|יְסַפֵּֽרוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Consume|כַּלֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb them in wrath;|בְחֵמָה֮\rb*
\q2 \rb consume them|כַּלֵּ֪ה\rb* \rb till they are no more,|וְֽאֵ֫ינֵ֥מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb so it may be known|וְֽיֵדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb to the ends|לְאַפְסֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֭לֹהִים\rb* \rb rules|מֹשֵׁ֣ל\rb* \rb over Jacob.|בְּיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb They return|וְיָשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb in the evening,|לָ֭עֶרֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb snarling|יֶהֱמ֥וּ\rb* \rb like dogs|כַכָּ֗לֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb and prowling around|וִיס֥וֹבְבוּ\rb* \rb the city.|עִֽיר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb They|הֵ֭מָּה\rb* \rb scavenge|יְנוּעוּן\rb* \rb for food,|לֶאֱכֹ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and growl|וַיָּלִֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb they are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb satisfied.|יִ֝שְׂבְּע֗וּ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֤י׀\rb* \rb will sing|אָשִׁ֣יר\rb* \rb of Your strength|עֻזֶּךָ֮\rb*
\q2 \rb and proclaim|וַאֲרַנֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb Your loving devotion|חַ֫סְדֶּ֥ךָ\rb* \rb in the morning.|לַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You are|הָיִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb my fortress,|מִשְׂגָּ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb my refuge|וּ֝מָנ֗וֹס\rb* \rb in times|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of trouble.|צַר־\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb To You,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O my strength,|עֻ֭זִּי\rb* \rb I sing praises,|אֲזַמֵּ֑רָה\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You, O God,|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb are my fortress,|מִ֝שְׂגַּבִּ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb my God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of loving devotion.|חַסְדִּֽי׃\rb*
\c 60
\s1 Victory with God
\r \ref 2 Samuel 8:1–14|2SA 8:1-14\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 18:1–13|1CH 18:1-13\ref*; \ref Psalm 108:1–13|PSA 108:1-13\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַ֭מְנַצֵּחַ\rb* \rb To the tune of|עַל־\rb* \rb “The Lily|שׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Covenant.”|עֵד֑וּת\rb* \rb A Miktam|מִכְתָּ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 60:1 \fqa Miktam\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 16|16\ref* and 56–60.\f* \rb of David|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb for instruction.|לְלַמֵּֽד׃\rb* \rb When he fought|בְּהַצּוֹת֨וֹ׀\rb*\rb |אֶ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb Aram-naharaim|נַהֲרַיִם֮\rb*\f + \fr 60:1 \ft That is, Mesopotamia; \fqa Aram-naharaim \ft means \fqa Aram of the two rivers\ft , likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia.\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֪ם\rb* \rb and Aram-zobah,|צ֫וֹבָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 60:1 \ft That is, the land northeast of Damascus\f* \rb and Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb and struck down|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb 12,000|שְׁנֵ֖ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb Edomites|אֱד֣וֹם\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵיא־\rb* \rb of Salt.|מֶ֑לַח\rb*
