\c 76
\s1 God’s Name Is Great in Israel
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb With stringed instruments.|בִּנְגִינֹ֑ת\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb of Asaph.|לְאָסָ֣ף\rb* \rb A song.|שִֽׁיר׃\rb*
\q1 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb is known|נוֹדָ֣ע\rb* \rb in Judah;|בִּֽיהוּדָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb His name|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is great|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּ֝יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb His tent|סֻכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb is|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb in Salem,|בְשָׁלֵ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 76:2 \ft That is, Jerusalem\f*
\q2 \rb His dwelling place|וּמְע֖וֹנָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb in Zion.|בְצִיּֽוֹן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb There|שָׁ֭מָּה\rb* \rb He shattered|שִׁבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb the flaming arrows,|רִשְׁפֵי־\rb*\rb |קָ֑שֶׁת\rb*
\q2 \rb the shield|מָגֵ֬ן\rb* \rb and sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and weapons of war.|וּמִלְחָמָ֣ה\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are resplendent with light,|נָ֭אוֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb more majestic|אַדִּ֗יר\rb* \rb than mountains|מֵֽהַרְרֵי־\rb* \rb filled with game.|טָֽרֶף׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb The valiant|אַבִּ֣ירֵי\rb*\rb |לֵ֭ב\rb* \rb lie plundered;|אֶשְׁתּוֹלְל֨וּ׀\rb* \rb they sleep|נָמ֣וּ\rb* \rb their last sleep.|שְׁנָתָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb No|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb of might|חַ֣יִל\rb* \rb could lift|מָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb a hand.|יְדֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb At Your rebuke,|מִ֭גַּעֲרָ֣תְךָ\rb* \rb O God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob,|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb both horse|וָסֽוּס׃\rb* \rb and rider|וְרֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb lie stunned.|נִ֝רְדָּ֗ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb alone|אַ֗תָּה\rb* \rb are to be feared.|נ֥וֹרָא\rb*
\q2 \rb When|מֵאָ֥ז\rb* \rb You are angry,|אַפֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb who|וּמִֽי־\rb* \rb can stand|יַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb before You?|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb From heaven|מִ֭שָּׁמַיִם\rb* \rb You pronounced|הִשְׁמַ֣עְתָּ\rb* \rb judgment,|דִּ֑ין\rb*
\q2 \rb and the earth|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb feared|יָֽרְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb and was still|וְשָׁקָֽטָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb when God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb rose up|בְּקוּם־\rb* \rb to judge,|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb*
\q2 \rb to save|לְהוֹשִׁ֖יעַ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the lowly|עַנְוֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth.|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Even|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the wrath|חֲמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb shall praise You;|תּוֹדֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb with the survivors|שְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of wrath|חֵמֹ֣ת\rb* \rb You will clothe Yourself.|תַּחְגֹּֽר׃\rb*\f + \fr 76:10 \ft Or \fqa Surely Your wrath against men brings You praise, and the survivors of Your wrath will be restrained.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Make|נִֽדֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb and fulfill your vows|וְשַׁלְּמוּ֮\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֪ה\rb* \rb your God;|אֱ‍ֽלֹהֵ֫יכֶ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the neighboring lands|סְבִיבָ֑יו\rb* \rb bring|יוֹבִ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb tribute|שַׁ֝֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb to Him who is to be feared.|לַמּוֹרָֽא׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb He breaks|יִ֭בְצֹר\rb* \rb the spirits|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of princes;|נְגִידִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb He is feared|נ֝וֹרָ֗א\rb* \rb by the kings|לְמַלְכֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth.|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\c 77
\s1 In the Day of Trouble I Sought the Lord
\d \v 1 \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb According to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jeduthun.|יְדִיתוּן\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb of Asaph.|לְאָסָ֥ף\rb*
\q1 \rb I cried out|קוֹלִ֣י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God;|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb I cried aloud|וְאֶצְעָ֑קָה\rb*\rb |קוֹלִ֥י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb to hear|וְהַאֲזִ֥ין\rb* \rb me.|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb In the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of trouble|צָרָתִי֮\rb* \rb I sought|דָּ֫רָ֥שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb the Lord;|אֲדֹנָ֪י\rb*
\q2 \rb through the night|לַ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb my outstretched hands|יָדִ֤י׀\rb*\rb |נִ֭גְּרָה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb did not grow weary;|תָפ֑וּג\rb*
\q2 \rb my soul|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb refused|מֵאֲנָ֖ה\rb* \rb to be comforted.|הִנָּחֵ֣ם\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb I remembered You,|אֶזְכְּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb O God,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and I groaned;|וְאֶֽהֱמָיָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I mused|אָשִׂ֓יחָה׀\rb* \rb and my spirit|רוּחִ֣י\rb* \rb grew faint.|וְתִתְעַטֵּ֖ף\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb You have kept|אָ֭חַזְתָּ\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינָ֑י\rb* \rb from closing;|שְׁמֻר֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb I am too troubled|נִ֝פְעַ֗מְתִּי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to speak.|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb I considered|חִשַּׁ֣בְתִּי\rb* \rb the days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb of old,|מִקֶּ֑דֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb the years|שְׁ֝נ֗וֹת\rb* \rb long in the past.|עוֹלָמִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb At night|בַּ֫לָּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb I remembered|אֶֽזְכְּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb my song;|נְגִינָתִ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb my heart|לְבָבִ֥י\rb* \rb I mused,|אָשִׂ֑יחָה\rb* \rb and my spirit|רוּחִֽי׃\rb* \rb pondered:|וַיְחַפֵּ֥שׂ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb “Will the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb spurn us|יִזְנַ֥ח׀\rb* \rb forever|הַֽ֭לְעוֹלָמִים\rb*
\q2 \rb and never|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יֹסִ֖יף\rb*\rb |עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb show His favor again?|לִרְצ֣וֹת\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Is His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb gone|הֶאָפֵ֣ס\rb* \rb forever?|לָנֶ֣צַח\rb*
\q2 \rb Has His promise|אֹ֝֗מֶר\rb* \rb failed|גָּ֥מַר\rb* \rb for all time?|לְדֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |וָדֹֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb Has God|אֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb forgotten|הֲשָׁכַ֣ח\rb* \rb to be gracious?|חַנּ֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb Has His anger|בְּ֝אַ֗ף\rb* \rb shut off|קָפַ֥ץ\rb* \rb His compassion?”|רַחֲמָ֥יו\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb So I said,|וָ֭אֹמַר\rb* \rb “I am grieved|חַלּ֣וֹתִי\rb*
\q2 \rb that the right hand|יְמִ֣ין\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb has changed.”|הִ֑יא\rb*\f + \fr 77:10 \ft Or \fqa “To this I will appeal: to the years of the right hand of the Most High.”\f*\rb |שְׁ֝נ֗וֹת\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb I will remember|אַזְכִּיר\rb* \rb the works|מַֽעַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb yes,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will remember|אֶזְכְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb Your wonders|פִּלְאֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb of old.|מִקֶּ֣דֶם\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will reflect|וְהָגִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb on all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb You have done|פָּעֳלֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and ponder|אָשִֽׂיחָה׃\rb* \rb Your mighty deeds.|וּֽבַעֲלִ֖ילוֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Your way,|דַּרְכֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb O God,|אֱ֭לֹהִים\rb* \rb is holy.|בַּקֹּ֣דֶשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb What|מִי־\rb* \rb god|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb is so great|גָּ֝ד֗וֹל\rb* \rb as our God?|כֵּֽאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are the God|הָ֭אֵל\rb* \rb who works|עֹ֣שֵׂה\rb* \rb wonders;|פֶ֑לֶא\rb*
\q2 \rb You display|הוֹדַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb Your strength|עֻזֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb among the peoples.|בָעַמִּ֣ים\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb With power|בִּזְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb You redeemed|גָּאַ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb Your people,|עַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb and Joseph.|וְיוֹסֵ֣ף\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb The waters|מַּ֨יִם׀\rb* \rb saw You,|רָ֘א֤וּךָ\rb* \rb O God;|אֱ‍ֽלֹהִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb the waters|מַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb saw You|רָא֣וּךָ\rb* \rb and swirled;|יָחִ֑ילוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb even|אַ֝֗ף\rb* \rb the depths|תְהֹמֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb were shaken.|יִרְגְּז֥וּ\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb The clouds|עָב֗וֹת\rb* \rb poured down|זֹ֤רְמוּ\rb* \rb water;|מַ֨יִם׀\rb*
\q2 \rb the skies|שְׁחָקִ֑ים\rb* \rb resounded|נָתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb with thunder;|ק֭וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb |אַף־\rb* \rb Your arrows|חֲ֝צָצֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb flashed back and forth.|יִתְהַלָּֽכוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Your thunder|רַעַמְךָ֨׀\rb* \rb resounded|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb in the whirlwind;|בַּגַּלְגַּ֗ל\rb*
\q2 \rb the lightning|בְרָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb lit up|הֵאִ֣ירוּ\rb* \rb the world;|תֵּבֵ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb trembled|רָגְזָ֖ה\rb* \rb and quaked.|וַתִּרְעַ֣שׁ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Your path|דַּרְכֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb led through the sea,|בַּיָּ֤ם\rb*
\q2 \rb Your way|וּשְׁבִילֶיךָ\rb* \rb through the mighty|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb waters,|בְּמַ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb but Your footprints|וְ֝עִקְּבוֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb were not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to be found.|נֹדָֽעוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 77:19 \ft Or \fqa were unknown\f*
\q1 \v 20 \rb You led|נָחִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb Your people|עַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb like a flock|כַצֹּ֣אן\rb*
\q2 \rb by the hand|בְּֽיַד־\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb and Aaron.|וְאַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb*
\c 78
\s1 I Will Open My Mouth in Parables
\r \ref Matthew 13:34–35|MAT 13:34-35\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb A Maskil|מַשְׂכִּ֗יל\rb*\f + \fr 78:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f* \rb of Asaph.|לְאָ֫סָ֥ף\rb*
\q1 \rb Give ear,|הַאֲזִ֣ינָה\rb* \rb O my people,|עַ֭מִּי\rb* \rb to my instruction;|תּוֹרָתִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb listen|הַטּ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אָ֝זְנְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to the words|לְאִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of my mouth.|פִֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will open|אֶפְתְּחָ֣ה\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֑י\rb* \rb in parables;|בְמָשָׁ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb I will utter|אַבִּ֥יעָה\rb* \rb things hidden|חִ֝יד֗וֹת\rb* \rb from|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb the beginning,|קֶֽדֶם׃\rb*\f + \fr 78:2 \ft Or \fqa from ancient times\ft ; see also LXX; cited in \ref Matthew 13:35|MAT 13:35\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 3 \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁ֭מַעְנוּ\rb* \rb and known|וַנֵּדָעֵ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and our fathers|וַ֝אֲבוֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb have relayed|סִפְּרוּ־\rb* \rb to us.|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb We will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb hide|נְכַחֵ֨ד׀\rb* \rb them from their children|מִבְּנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb but will declare|מְֽ֭סַפְּרִים\rb* \rb to the next|אַחֲר֗וֹן\rb* \rb generation|לְד֥וֹר\rb*
\q1 \rb the praises|תְּהִלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and His might|וֶעֱזוּז֥וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the wonders|וְ֝נִפְלְאוֹתָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has performed.|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb For He established|וַיָּ֤קֶם\rb* \rb a testimony|עֵד֨וּת׀\rb* \rb in Jacob|בְּֽיַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*
\q2 \rb and appointed|שָׂ֤ם\rb* \rb a law|וְתוֹרָה֮\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָ֫אֵ֥ל\rb*
\q1 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He commanded|צִ֭וָּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to teach|לְ֝הוֹדִיעָ֗ם\rb* \rb to their children,|לִבְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb the coming|אַ֭חֲרוֹן\rb* \rb generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb would know them—|יֵדְע֨וּ׀\rb*
\q2 \rb even children|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb yet to be born—|יִוָּלֵ֑דוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to arise|יָ֝קֻ֗מוּ\rb* \rb and tell|וִֽיסַפְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb their own children|לִבְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb that they should put|וְיָשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb their confidence|כִּ֫סְלָ֥ם\rb* \rb in God,|בֵֽאלֹהִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb forgetting|יִ֭שְׁכְּחוּ\rb* \rb His|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb works,|מַֽעַלְלֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb but keeping|יִנְצֹֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb His commandments.|וּמִצְוֺתָ֥יו\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Then they will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֨וּ׀\rb* \rb like their fathers,|כַּאֲבוֹתָ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb a stubborn|סוֹרֵ֪ר\rb* \rb and rebellious|וּמֹ֫רֶ֥ה\rb* \rb generation,|דּוֹר֮\rb*
\q1 \rb |דּ֭וֹר\rb* \rb whose heart|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb was not|לֹא־\rb* \rb loyal,|הֵכִ֣ין\rb*
\q2 \rb whose spirit|רוּחֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb was not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb faithful|נֶאֶמְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb God.|אֵ֣ל\rb*
