\q1 \v 6 \rb Hear|הַאֲזִ֣ינָה\rb* \rb my prayer,|תְּפִלָּתִ֑י\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb and attend|וְ֝הַקְשִׁ֗יבָה\rb* \rb to my plea|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb for mercy.|תַּחֲנוּנוֹתָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb In the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of my distress|צָ֭רָתִ֥י\rb* \rb I call on You,|אֶקְרָאֶ֗ךָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You answer me.|תַעֲנֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb* \rb there is none|אֵין־\rb* \rb like You|כָּמ֖וֹךָ\rb* \rb among the gods,|בָאֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb*
\q2 \rb nor any|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb works like Yours.|כְּֽמַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיִ֤ם׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have made|עָשִׂ֗יתָ\rb*
\q2 \rb will come|יָב֤וֹאוּ׀\rb* \rb and bow|וְיִשְׁתַּחֲו֣וּ\rb* \rb before You,|לְפָנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and they will glorify|וִֽיכַבְּד֣וּ\rb* \rb Your name.|לִשְׁמֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb are great|גָד֣וֹל\rb* \rb and perform|וְעֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb wonders;|נִפְלָא֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb are God.|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Teach me|ה֘וֹרֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb Your way,|דַּרְכֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb*
\q2 \rb that I may walk|אֲהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Your truth.|בַּאֲמִתֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Give me an undivided|יַחֵ֥ד\rb* \rb heart,|לְ֝בָבִ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb that I may fear|לְיִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb Your name.|שְׁמֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will praise You,|אוֹדְךָ֤׀\rb* \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb my God,|אֱ֭לֹהַי\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb my heart;|לְבָבִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb I will glorify|וַאֲכַבְּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb Your name|שִׁמְךָ֣\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb great is|גָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb Your loving devotion|חַ֭סְדְּךָ\rb* \rb to me;|עָלָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb You have delivered|וְהִצַּ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb me|נַ֝פְשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb from the depths|תַּחְתִּיָּֽה׃\rb* \rb of Sheol.|מִשְּׁא֥וֹל\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The arrogant|זֵ֘דִ֤ים\rb* \rb rise|קָֽמוּ־\rb* \rb against me,|עָלַ֗י\rb* \rb O God;|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb*
\q2 \rb a band|וַעֲדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of ruthless men|עָ֭רִיצִים\rb* \rb seeks|בִּקְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb my life;|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb they have no|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb regard|שָׂמ֣וּךָ\rb* \rb for You.|לְנֶגְדָּֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb But You,|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb O Lord,|אֲ֭דֹנָי\rb* \rb are a compassionate|רַח֣וּם\rb* \rb and gracious|וְחַנּ֑וּן\rb* \rb God,|אֵל־\rb*
\q2 \rb slow|אֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to anger,|אַ֝פַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb abounding|וְרַב־\rb* \rb in loving devotion|חֶ֥סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness.|וֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Turn|פְּנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb and have mercy;|וְחָ֫נֵּ֥נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb grant|תְּנָֽה־\rb* \rb Your strength|עֻזְּךָ֥\rb* \rb to Your servant;|לְעַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb save|וְ֝הוֹשִׁ֗יעָה\rb* \rb the son|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb of Your maidservant.|אֲמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb Show|עֲשֵֽׂה־\rb* \rb me|עִמִּ֥י\rb* \rb a sign|א֗וֹת\rb* \rb of Your goodness,|לְט֫וֹבָ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb that my enemies|שֹׂנְאַ֣י\rb* \rb may see|וְיִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and be ashamed;|וְיֵבֹ֑שׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You,|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb* \rb have helped me|עֲזַרְתַּ֥נִי\rb* \rb and comforted me.|וְנִחַמְתָּֽנִי׃\rb*
\c 87
\s1 The LORD Loves the Gates of Zion
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the sons|לִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Korah.|קֹ֭רַח\rb* \rb A song.|שִׁ֑יר\rb*
\q1 \rb He has founded His city|יְ֝סוּדָת֗וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb on the holy|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb mountains.|בְּהַרְרֵי־\rb*\f + \fr 87:1 \ft Literally \fqa His foundation is on the holy mountains\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb loves|אֹהֵ֣ב\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb more than all|מִ֝כֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb the dwellings|מִשְׁכְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jacob.|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Glorious things|נִ֭כְבָּדוֹת\rb* \rb are ascribed|מְדֻבָּ֣ר\rb* \rb to you,|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb O city|עִ֖יר\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb “I will mention|אַזְכִּ֤יר׀\rb* \rb Rahab|רַ֥הַב\rb*\f + \fr 87:4 \fqa Rahab \ft is a poetic name for Egypt.\f* \rb and Babylon|וּבָבֶ֗ל\rb*
\q2 \rb among those who know Me—|לְֽיֹ֫דְעָ֥י\rb*
\q1 \rb along with|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Philistia,|פְלֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Tyre,|וְצ֣וֹר\rb* \rb and|עִם־\rb* \rb Cush|כּ֑וּשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 87:4 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* —
\q2 \rb when I say, ‘This one|זֶ֝֗ה\rb* \rb was born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb in Zion.’”|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb And it will be said|יֵאָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb of Zion:|וּֽלֲצִיּ֨וֹן׀\rb*
\q2 \rb “This one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and that one|וְ֭אִישׁ\rb* \rb were born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb in her,|בָּ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the Most High|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Himself|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will establish her.”|יְכוֹנְנֶ֣הָ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb The LORD|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb will record|יִ֭סְפֹּר\rb* \rb in the register|בִּכְת֣וֹב\rb* \rb of the peoples:|עַמִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb “This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb one was born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb in Zion.”|שָׁ֣ם\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Singers|וְשָׁרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and pipers will proclaim,|כְּחֹלְלִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb “All|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb my springs of joy|מַעְיָנַ֥י\rb* \rb are in You.”|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\c 88
\s1 I Cry Out before You
\d \v 1 \rb A song.|שִׁ֥יר\rb* \rb A Psalm|מִזְמ֗וֹר\rb* \rb of the sons|לִבְנֵ֫י\rb* \rb of Korah.|קֹ֥רַח\rb* \rb For the choirmaster.|לַמְנַצֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb According to|עַל־\rb* \rb Mahalath|מָחֲלַ֣ת\rb* \rb Leannoth.|לְעַנּ֑וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 88:1 \fqa Mahalath Leannoth\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; see also \ref Psalm 53:1|PSA 53:1\ref*.\f* \rb A Maskil|מַ֝שְׂכִּ֗יל\rb*\f + \fr 88:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f* \rb of Heman|לְהֵימָ֥ן\rb* \rb the Ezrahite.|הָאֶזְרָחִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my salvation,|יְשׁוּעָתִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb and night|בַלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb I cry out|צָעַ֖קְתִּי\rb* \rb before You.|נֶגְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb May my prayer|תְּפִלָּתִ֑י\rb* \rb come|תָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb before You;|לְ֭פָנֶיךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb incline|הַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb Your ear|אָ֝זְנְךָ֗\rb* \rb to my cry.|לְרִנָּתִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb is full|שָֽׂבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb of troubles,|בְרָע֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and my life|וְחַיַּ֗י\rb* \rb draws near|הִגִּֽיעוּ׃\rb* \rb to Sheol.|לִשְׁא֥וֹל\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb I am counted|נֶ֭חְשַׁבְתִּי\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb those descending|י֣וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit.|ב֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb I am|הָ֝יִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb like a man|כְּגֶ֣בֶר\rb* \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb strength.|אֱיָֽל׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb I am forsaken|חָ֫פְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb among the dead,|בַּמֵּתִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb like|כְּמ֤וֹ\rb* \rb the slain|חֲלָלִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb who lie|שֹׁ֥כְבֵי\rb* \rb in the grave,|קֶ֗בֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb You|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb remember|זְכַרְתָּ֣ם\rb* \rb no more,|ע֑וֹד\rb*
\q2 \rb who|וְ֝הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb are cut off|נִגְזָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb from Your care.|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb You have laid me|שַׁ֭תַּנִי\rb* \rb in the lowest|תַּחְתִּיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb Pit,|בְּב֣וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb in the darkest|בְּ֝מַחֲשַׁכִּ֗ים\rb* \rb of the depths.|בִּמְצֹלֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Your wrath|חֲמָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb weighs heavily|סָמְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb upon me;|עָ֭לַי\rb*
\q2 \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Your waves|מִ֝שְׁבָּרֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb have submerged me.|עִנִּ֥יתָ\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶּֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb You have removed|הִרְחַ֥קְתָּ\rb* \rb my friends|מְיֻדָּעַ֗י\rb* \rb from me;|מִ֫מֶּ֥נִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb You have made me|שַׁתַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb repulsive|תוֹעֵב֣וֹת\rb* \rb to them;|לָ֑מוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb I am confined|כָּ֝לֻ֗א\rb* \rb and cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb escape.|אֵצֵֽא׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb My eyes|עֵינִ֥י\rb* \rb grow dim|דָאֲבָ֗ה\rb* \rb with|מִנִּ֫י\rb* \rb grief.|עֹ֥נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb I call to You|קְרָאתִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb daily,|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |י֑וֹם\rb* \rb O LORD;|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I spread out|שִׁטַּ֖חְתִּי\rb* \rb my hands|כַפָּֽי׃\rb* \rb to You.|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Do You work|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb wonders|פֶּ֑לֶא\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb for the dead?|הֲלַמֵּתִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb Do departed spirits|רְ֝פָאִ֗ים\rb* \rb rise up|יָק֤וּמוּ׀\rb* \rb to praise You?|יוֹד֬וּךָ\rb*
\qr \rb Selah|סֶּֽלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Can Your loving devotion|חַסְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb be proclaimed|הַיְסֻפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb in the grave,|בַּקֶּ֣בֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb Your faithfulness|אֱ֝מֽוּנָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb in Abaddon|בָּאֲבַדּֽוֹן׃\rb*\f + \fr 88:11 \fqa Abaddon \ft means \fqa Destruction\ft .\f*?
\q1 \v 12 \rb Will Your wonders|פִּלְאֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb be known|הֲיִוָּדַ֣ע\rb* \rb in the darkness,|בַּחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb or Your righteousness|וְ֝צִדְקָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of oblivion?|נְשִׁיָּֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb But|וַאֲנִ֤י׀\rb* \rb to You,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb I cry for help;|שִׁוַּ֑עְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb in the morning|וּ֝בַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb my prayer|תְּֽפִלָּתִ֥י\rb* \rb comes before You.|תְקַדְּמֶֽךָּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb Why,|לָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb do You reject|תִּזְנַ֣ח\rb* \rb me?|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb Why do You hide|תַּסְתִּ֖יר\rb* \rb Your face|פָּנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb from me?|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb From my youth|מִנֹּ֑עַר\rb* \rb I was|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb afflicted|עָ֘נִ֤י\rb* \rb and near death.|וְגֹוֵ֣עַ\rb*
\q2 \rb I have borne|נָשָׂ֖אתִי\rb* \rb Your terrors;|אֵמֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb I am in despair.|אָפֽוּנָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Your wrath|חֲרוֹנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb has swept|עָבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb over me;|עָ֭לַי\rb*
\q2 \rb Your terrors|בִּ֝עוּתֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb have destroyed me.|צִמְּתוּתֻֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb they engulf me|סַבּ֣וּנִי\rb* \rb like water;|כַ֭מַּיִם\rb*
\q2 \rb they enclose me|הִקִּ֖יפוּ\rb* \rb on|עָלַ֣י\rb* \rb every side.|יָֽחַד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb You have removed|הִרְחַ֣קְתָּ\rb* \rb my|מִ֭מֶּנִּי\rb* \rb beloved|אֹהֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and my friend;|וָרֵ֑עַ\rb*
\q2 \rb darkness|מַחְשָֽׁךְ׃\rb* \rb is my closest companion.|מְֽיֻדָּעַ֥י\rb*
\c 89
\s1 I Will Sing of His Love Forever
\d \v 1 \rb A Maskil|מַ֝שְׂכִּ֗יל\rb*\f + \fr 89:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f* \rb of Ethan|לְאֵיתָ֥ן\rb* \rb the Ezrahite.|הָֽאֶזְרָחִֽי׃\rb*
