\c 90
\ms BOOK IV
\d Psalms 90–106
\s1 From Everlasting to Everlasting
\d \v 1 \rb A prayer|תְּפִלָּה֮\rb* \rb of Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֪ה\rb* \rb the man|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹ֫הִ֥ים\rb*
\q1 \rb Lord,|אֲ‍ֽדֹנָ֗י\rb* \rb You|אַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb have been|הָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb our|לָּ֗נוּ\rb* \rb dwelling place|מָע֣וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb through all|בְּדֹ֣ר\rb* \rb generations.|וָדֹֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Before|בְּטֶ֤רֶם׀\rb* \rb the mountains|הָ֘רִ֤ים\rb* \rb were born|יֻלָּ֗דוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb or You brought forth|וַתְּח֣וֹלֵֽל\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and the world,|וְתֵבֵ֑ל\rb*
\q1 \rb from everlasting|וּֽמֵעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb everlasting|ע֝וֹלָ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are God.|אֵֽל׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb You return|תָּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb man|אֱ֭נוֹשׁ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb dust,|דַּכָּ֑א\rb*
\q2 \rb saying,|וַ֝תֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Return,|שׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb O sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of mortals.”|אָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb in Your sight|בְּֽעֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֪לֶף\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֡ים\rb*
\q2 \rb are but|כְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb a day|אֶ֭תְמוֹל\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb passes,|יַעֲבֹ֑ר\rb*\f + \fr 90:4 \ft \ref See 2|2\ref* Peter 3:8.\f*
\q2 \rb or a watch|וְאַשְׁמוּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb of the night.|בַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You sweep them away|זְ֭רַמְתָּם\rb* \rb in their sleep;|שֵׁנָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb they are|יִהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb like the new grass|כֶּחָצִ֥יר\rb*\rb |יַחֲלֹֽף׃\rb* \rb of the morning—|בַּ֝בֹּ֗קֶר\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb in the morning|בַּ֭בֹּקֶר\rb* \rb it springs up|יָצִ֣יץ\rb* \rb new,|וְחָלָ֑ף\rb*
\q2 \rb but by evening|לָ֝עֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb it fades|יְמוֹלֵ֥ל\rb* \rb and withers.|וְיָבֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we are consumed|כָלִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb by Your anger|בְאַפֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and terrified|נִבְהָֽלְנוּ׃\rb* \rb by Your wrath.|וּֽבַחֲמָתְךָ֥\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb You have set|שַׁתָּ\rb* \rb our iniquities|עֲוֺנֹתֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb before You,|לְנֶגְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb our secret sins|עֲ֝לֻמֵ֗נוּ\rb* \rb in the light|לִמְא֥וֹר\rb* \rb of Your presence.|פָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb our days|יָ֭מֵינוּ\rb* \rb decline|פָּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb in Your fury;|בְעֶבְרָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb we finish|כִּלִּ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb our years|שָׁנֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb with|כְמוֹ־\rb* \rb a sigh.|הֶֽגֶה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb The length of our days|יְמֵֽי־\rb*\rb |שְׁנוֹתֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb is seventy|שִׁבְעִ֪ים\rb* \rb years—|שָׁנָ֡ה\rb*
\q2 \rb or eighty|שְׁמ֘וֹנִ֤ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb if we are strong—|וְאִ֤ם\rb*\rb |בִּגְבוּרֹ֨ת׀\rb*
\q1 \rb yet their pride|וְ֭רָהְבָּם\rb* \rb is but labor|עָמָ֣ל\rb* \rb and sorrow,|וָאָ֑וֶן\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb they quickly|חִ֝֗ישׁ\rb* \rb pass,|גָ֥ז\rb* \rb and we fly away.|וַנָּעֻֽפָה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb knows|י֭וֹדֵעַ\rb* \rb the power|עֹ֣ז\rb* \rb of Your anger?|אַפֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb Your wrath|עֶבְרָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb matches the fear You are due.|וּ֝כְיִרְאָתְךָ֗\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb So|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb teach us|הוֹדַ֑ע\rb* \rb to number|לִמְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb our days,|יָ֭מֵינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that we may present|וְ֝נָבִ֗א\rb* \rb a heart|לְבַ֣ב\rb* \rb of wisdom.|חָכְמָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Return,|שׁוּבָ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD!|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb How long will it be?|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb Have compassion|וְ֝הִנָּחֵ֗ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Your servants.|עֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb Satisfy us|שַׂבְּעֵ֣נוּ\rb* \rb in the morning|בַבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb with Your loving devotion,|חַסְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb that we may sing for joy|וּֽנְרַנְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb and be glad|וְ֝נִשְׂמְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb our days.|יָמֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Make us glad|שַׂ֭מְּחֵנוּ\rb* \rb for as many days|כִּימ֣וֹת\rb* \rb as You have afflicted us,|עִנִּיתָ֑נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for as many years|שְׁ֝נ֗וֹת\rb* \rb as we have seen|רָאִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb evil.|רָעָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb May Your work|פָעֳלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb be shown|יֵרָאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your servants,|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your splendor|וַ֝הֲדָרְךָ֗\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their children.|בְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb May the favor|נֹ֤עַם\rb*\f + \fr 90:17 \ft Or \fqa beauty\f* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb rest|וִיהִ֤י׀\rb* \rb upon us;|עָ֫לֵ֥ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb establish|כּוֹנְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb for us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb the work|וּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of our hands—|יָ֭דֵינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb yes, establish|כּוֹנְנֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb the work|וּֽמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of our hands!|יָ֝דֵ֗ינוּ\rb*
\c 91
\s1 You Are My Refuge and My Fortress
\q1 \v 1 \rb He who dwells|יֹ֭שֵׁב\rb* \rb in the shelter|בְּסֵ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְי֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb will abide|יִתְלוֹנָֽן׃\rb* \rb in the shadow|בְּצֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of the Almighty.|שַׁ֝דַּ֗י\rb*\f + \fr 91:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shaddai\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will say|אֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽ֭יהוָה\rb* \rb “You are my refuge|מַחְסִ֣י\rb* \rb and my fortress,|וּמְצוּדָתִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb my God,|אֱ֝לֹהַ֗י\rb* \rb in whom I trust.”|אֶבְטַח־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Surely|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will deliver you|יַ֭צִּֽילְךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb from the snare|מִפַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of the fowler,|יָק֗וּשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and from the deadly|הַוּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb plague.|מִדֶּ֥בֶר\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb He will cover|יָ֣סֶךְ\rb* \rb you|לָ֭ךְ\rb* \rb with His feathers;|בְּאֶבְרָת֨וֹ׀\rb*
\q2 \rb under|וְתַֽחַת־\rb* \rb His wings|כְּנָפָ֣יו\rb* \rb you will find refuge;|תֶּחְסֶ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb His faithfulness|אֲמִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is a shield|צִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and rampart.|וְֽסֹחֵרָ֣ה\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb fear|תִ֭ירָא\rb* \rb the terror|מִפַּ֣חַד\rb* \rb of the night,|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb nor the arrow|מֵ֝חֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb that flies|יָע֥וּף\rb* \rb by day,|יוֹמָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb nor the pestilence|מִ֭דֶּבֶר\rb* \rb that stalks|יַהֲלֹ֑ךְ\rb* \rb in the darkness,|בָּאֹ֣פֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb nor the calamity|מִ֝קֶּ֗טֶב\rb* \rb that destroys|יָשׁ֥וּד\rb* \rb at noon.|צָהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Though a thousand|אֶ֗לֶף\rb* \rb may fall|יִפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb at your side,|מִצִּדְּךָ֨׀\rb*
\q2 \rb and ten thousand|וּרְבָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb at your right hand,|מִימִינֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb no harm|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb will come near|אֵ֝לֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb you.|יִגָּֽשׁ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb You will only|רַ֭ק\rb* \rb see it|תַבִּ֑יט\rb* \rb with your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and witness|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb the punishment|וְשִׁלֻּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the wicked.|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have made|שַׂ֣מְתָּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your dwelling—|מְעוֹנֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb my refuge,|מַחְסִ֑י\rb* \rb the Most High—|עֶ֝לְי֗וֹן\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb will befall|תְאֻנֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb you,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb plague|וְ֝נֶ֗גַע\rb* \rb will approach|יִקְרַ֥ב\rb* \rb your tent.|בְּאָהֳלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He will command|יְצַוֶּה־\rb* \rb His angels|מַ֭לְאָכָיו\rb* \rb concerning you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb to guard you|לִ֝שְׁמָרְךָ֗\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your ways.|דְּרָכֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb They will lift you up|יִשָּׂא֑וּנְךָ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their hands,|כַּפַּ֥יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb so that you will not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb strike|תִּגֹּ֖ף\rb* \rb your foot|רַגְלֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb against a stone.|בָּאֶ֣בֶן\rb*\f + \fr 91:12 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 4:6|MAT 4:6\ref* and Luke 4:10–11\f*
\q1 \v 13 \rb You will tread|תִּדְרֹ֑ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the lion|שַׁ֣חַל\rb* \rb and cobra;|וָפֶ֣תֶן\rb*
\q2 \rb you will trample|תִּרְמֹ֖ס\rb* \rb the young lion|כְּפִ֣יר\rb* \rb and serpent.|וְתַנִּֽין׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb “Because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he loves|חָ֭שַׁק\rb* \rb Me,|בִ֣י\rb* \rb I will deliver him;|וַאֲפַלְּטֵ֑הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he knows|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb My name,|שְׁמִֽי׃\rb* \rb I will protect him.|אֲ֝שַׂגְּבֵ֗הוּ\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb When he calls out to Me,|יִקְרָאֵ֨נִי׀\rb*
\q2 \rb I will answer him;|וְֽאֶעֱנֵ֗הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb will be with him|עִמּֽוֹ־\rb* \rb in trouble.|בְצָרָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I will deliver him|אֲ֝חַלְּצֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and honor him.|וַֽאֲכַבְּדֵֽהוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb With long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb life|יָ֭מִים\rb* \rb I will satisfy him|אַשְׂבִּיעֵ֑הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and show him|וְ֝אַרְאֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb My salvation.”|בִּֽישׁוּעָתִֽי׃\rb*
\c 92
\s1 How Great Are Your Works!
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm.|מִזְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb A song|שִׁ֗יר\rb* \rb for the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃\rb* \rb day.|לְי֣וֹם\rb*
\q1 \rb It is good|ט֗וֹב\rb* \rb to praise|לְהֹד֥וֹת\rb* \rb the LORD,|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and to sing praises|וּלְזַמֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to Your name,|לְשִׁמְךָ֣\rb* \rb O Most High,|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb to proclaim|לְהַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb Your loving devotion|חַסְֽדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your faithfulness|וֶ֝אֱמֽוּנָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb at night|בַּלֵּילֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb with|עֲ‍ֽלֵי־\rb* \rb the ten-stringed|עָ֭שׂוֹר\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵי־\rb* \rb harp|נָ֑בֶל\rb*\rb |עֲלֵ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb and the melody|הִגָּי֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the lyre.|בְּכִנּֽוֹר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb You, O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb have made me glad|שִׂמַּחְתַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb by Your deeds;|בְּפָעֳלֶ֑ךָ\rb*
