\q1 \rb stood|עָמַ֣ד\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb in the breach|בַּפֶּ֣רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb to divert|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb His wrath|חֲ֝מָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb from destroying them.|מֵֽהַשְׁחִֽית׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb They despised|וַֽ֭יִּמְאֲסוּ\rb* \rb the pleasant|חֶמְדָּ֑ה\rb* \rb land;|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb believe|הֶ֝אֱמִ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb His promise.|לִדְבָרֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 25 \rb They grumbled|וַיֵּרָגְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb in their tents|בְאָהֳלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁ֝מְע֗וּ\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 26 \rb So He raised|וַיִּשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb His hand|יָד֣וֹ\rb* \rb and swore|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb to cast them down|לְהַפִּ֥יל\rb*\rb |א֝וֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 27 \rb to disperse|וּלְהַפִּ֣יל\rb*\f + \fr 106:27 \ft Or \fqa cast down \ft or \fqa cause to fall\f* \rb their offspring|זַ֭רְעָם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and scatter them|וּ֝לְזָרוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb throughout the lands.|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb They yoked themselves|וַ֭יִּצָּ֣מְדוּ\rb*\rb |לְבַ֣עַל\rb* \rb to Baal of Peor|פְּע֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb and ate|וַ֝יֹּאכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זִבְחֵ֥י\rb* \rb offered to lifeless gods.|מֵתִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 29 \rb So they provoked the LORD to anger|וַ֭יַּכְעִיסוּ\rb* \rb with their deeds,|בְּמַֽעַלְלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and a plague|מַגֵּפָֽה׃\rb* \rb broke out|וַתִּפְרָץ־\rb* \rb among them.|בָּ֝֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 30 \rb But Phinehas|פִּֽ֭ינְחָס\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb and intervened,|וַיְפַלֵּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָֽה׃\rb* \rb was restrained.|וַ֝תֵּעָצַ֗ר\rb*
\q1 \v 31 \rb It was credited|וַתֵּחָ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb to him|ל֭וֹ\rb* \rb as righteousness|לִצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb for endless|לְדֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb generations|וָ֝דֹ֗ר\rb* \rb to come.|עַד־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb At the waters|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Meribah|מְרִיבָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 106:32 \fqa Meribah \ft means \fqa quarreling\ft ; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*.\f* \rb they angered|וַ֭יַּקְצִיפוּ\rb* \rb the LORD,|עַל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and trouble came|וַיֵּ֥רַע\rb* \rb to Moses|לְ֝מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb because of them.|בַּעֲבוּרָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 33 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they rebelled against|הִמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His Spirit,|רוּח֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 106:33 \ft Or \fqa they provoked His Spirit\f*
\q2 \rb and Moses spoke rashly|וַ֝יְבַטֵּ֗א\rb* \rb with his lips.|בִּשְׂפָתָֽיו׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 34 \rb They did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb destroy|הִ֭שְׁמִידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb had commanded|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 35 \rb but they mingled|וַיִּתְעָרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb with the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and adopted|וַֽ֝יִּלְמְד֗וּ\rb* \rb their customs.|מַֽעֲשֵׂיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 36 \rb They worshiped|וַיַּעַבְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their idols,|עֲצַבֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb which became|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb a snare to them.|לְמוֹקֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 37 \rb They sacrificed|וַיִּזְבְּח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their sons|בְּ֭נֵיהֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their daughters|בְּנֽוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to demons.|לַשֵּֽׁדִים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 38 \rb They shed|וַיִּֽשְׁפְּכ֨וּ\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֡י\rb* \rb blood—|דָ֪ם\rb*
\q2 \rb the blood|דַּם־\rb* \rb of their sons|בְּנֵ֘יהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּֽבְנוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they sacrificed|זִ֭בְּחוּ\rb* \rb to the idols|לַעֲצַבֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of Canaan,|כְנָ֑עַן\rb*
\q2 \rb and the land|הָ֝אָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb was polluted|וַתֶּחֱנַ֥ף\rb* \rb with blood.|בַּדָּמִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 39 \rb They defiled themselves|וַיִּטְמְא֥וּ\rb* \rb by their actions|בְמַעֲשֵׂיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and prostituted themselves|וַ֝יִּזְנוּ֗\rb* \rb by their deeds.|בְּמַֽעַלְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 40 \rb So the anger|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against His people,|בְּעַמּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and He abhorred|וַ֝יְתָעֵ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His own inheritance.|נַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 41 \rb He delivered them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the nations,|גּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and those who hated them|שֹׂנְאֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb ruled|וַֽיִּמְשְׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb over them.|בָ֝הֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 42 \rb Their enemies|אוֹיְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb oppressed them|וַיִּלְחָצ֥וּם\rb*
\q2 \rb and subdued them|וַ֝יִּכָּנְע֗וּ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb their hand.|יָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 43 \rb Many|רַבּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb He rescued them,|יַצִּ֫ילֵ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb but they|וְ֭הֵמָּה\rb* \rb were bent|יַמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb on rebellion|בַעֲצָתָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and sank down|וַ֝יָּמֹ֗כּוּ\rb* \rb in their iniquity.|בַּעֲוֺנָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 44 \rb Nevertheless He heard|בְּ֝שָׁמְע֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their cry;|רִנָּתָֽם׃\rb*
\q2 \rb He took note|וַ֭יַּרְא\rb* \rb of their distress.|בַּצַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \v 45 \rb And He remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֑וֹ\rb* \rb with them,|לָהֶ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and relented|וַ֝יִּנָּחֵ֗ם\rb* \rb by the abundance|כְּרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb of His loving devotion.|חַסְדּוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 46 \rb He made|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb objects of compassion|לְרַחֲמִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb to|לִ֝פְנֵ֗י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who held them captive.|שׁוֹבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 47 \rb Save us,|הוֹשִׁיעֵ֨נוּ׀\rb* \rb O LORD|יְה֘וָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and gather us|וְקַבְּצֵנוּ֮\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb the nations,|הַגּ֫וֹיִ֥ם\rb*
\q1 \rb that we may give thanks|לְ֭הֹדוֹת\rb* \rb to Your holy|קָדְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb name,|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb that we may glory|לְ֝הִשְׁתַּבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb in Your praise.|בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 48 \rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֪י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb*
\q2 \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb everlasting|הָ֤עוֹלָ֨ם׀\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֬ד\rb* \rb everlasting.|הָעוֹלָ֗ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb “Amen!”|אָמֵ֗ן\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Hallelujah!|הַֽלְלוּ־\rb*\rb |יָֽהּ׃\rb*
\c 107
\ms BOOK V
\d Psalms 107–150
\s1 Thanksgiving for Deliverance
\r \ref Matthew 8:23–27|MAT 8:23-27\ref*; \ref Mark 4:35–41|MRK 4:35-41\ref*; \ref Luke 8:22–25|LUK 8:22-25\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Give thanks|הֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb He is good;|ט֑וֹב\rb*\rb |כִּ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb endures forever.|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Let the redeemed|גְּאוּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb say so,|יֹ֭אמְרוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has redeemed|גְּ֝אָלָ֗ם\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּד־\rb* \rb of the enemy|צָֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb and gathered|קִ֫בְּצָ֥ם\rb* \rb from the lands,|וּֽמֵאֲרָצ֗וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb from east|מִמִּזְרָ֥ח\rb* \rb and west,|וּמִֽמַּעֲרָ֑ב\rb* \rb from north|מִצָּפ֥וֹן\rb* \rb and south.|וּמִיָּֽם׃\rb*\f + \fr 107:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa north and the sea\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Some wandered|תָּע֣וּ\rb* \rb in desert|בַ֭מִּדְבָּר\rb* \rb wastelands,|בִּישִׁימ֣וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb finding|מָצָֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb path|דָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb to a city|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb in which to dwell.|מ֝וֹשָׁ֗ב\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb They were hungry|רְעֵבִ֥ים\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb thirsty;|צְמֵאִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb their soul|נַ֝פְשָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb fainted|תִּתְעַטָּֽף׃\rb* \rb within them.|בָּהֶ֥ם\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Then they cried out|וַיִּצְעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb in their trouble,|בַּצַּ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and He delivered|יַצִּילֵֽם׃\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb from their distress.|מִ֝מְּצֽוּקוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb He led them|וַ֭יַּֽדְרִיכֵם\rb* \rb on a straight|יְשָׁרָ֑ה\rb* \rb path|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb to reach|לָ֝לֶ֗כֶת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a city|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb where they could live.|מוֹשָֽׁב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Let them give thanks|יוֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb for His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and His wonders|וְ֝נִפְלְאוֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb to the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men.|אָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb He satisfies|הִ֭שְׂבִּיעַ\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb the thirsty|שֹׁקֵקָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and fills|מִלֵּא־\rb*\rb |וְנֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb the hungry|רְ֝עֵבָה\rb* \rb with good things.|טֽוֹב׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Some sat|יֹ֭שְׁבֵי\rb* \rb in darkness|חֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and in the shadow of death,|וְצַלְמָ֑וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb prisoners|אֲסִירֵ֖י\rb* \rb in affliction|עֳנִ֣י\rb* \rb and chains,|וּבַרְזֶֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they rebelled|הִמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb against the words|אִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of God|אֵ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and despised|נָאָֽצוּ׃\rb* \rb the counsel|וַעֲצַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Most High.|עֶלְי֣וֹן\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb He humbled|וַיַּכְנַ֣ע\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֑ם\rb* \rb with hard labor;|בֶּעָמָ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb they stumbled,|כָּ֝שְׁל֗וּ\rb* \rb and there was no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one to help.|עֹזֵֽר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Then they cried out|וַיִּזְעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb in their trouble,|בַּצַּ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and He saved|יוֹשִׁיעֵֽם׃\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb from their distress.|מִ֝מְּצֻֽקוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb He brought them out|יֽ֭וֹצִיאֵם\rb* \rb of darkness|מֵחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and the shadow of death|וְצַלְמָ֑וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb and broke away their chains.|וּמוֹסְר֖וֹתֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |יְנַתֵּֽק׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Let them give thanks|יוֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb for His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and His wonders|וְ֝נִפְלְאוֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb to the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men.|אָדָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He has broken down|שִׁ֭בַּר\rb* \rb the gates|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb*
\q2 \rb and cut through|גִּדֵּֽעַ׃\rb* \rb the bars|וּבְרִיחֵ֖י\rb* \rb of iron.|בַרְזֶ֣ל\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Fools,|אֱ֭וִלִים\rb* \rb in their rebellious|פִּשְׁעָ֑ם\rb* \rb ways,|מִדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and through their iniquities,|וּֽ֝מֵעֲוֺֽנֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb suffered affliction.|יִתְעַנּֽוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb They|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb loathed|תְּתַעֵ֣ב\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb food|אֹ֭כֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb and drew near|וַ֝יַּגִּ֗יעוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁ֥עֲרֵי\rb* \rb of death.|מָֽוֶת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb Then they cried out|וַיִּזְעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb in their trouble,|בַּצַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and He saved them|יוֹשִׁיעֵֽם׃\rb* \rb from their distress.|מִ֝מְּצֻֽקוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb He sent forth|יִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb His word|דְּ֭בָרוֹ\rb* \rb and healed them;|וְיִרְפָּאֵ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb He rescued them|וִֽ֝ימַלֵּ֗ט\rb* \rb from the Pit.|מִשְּׁחִיתוֹתָֽם׃׆\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb Let them give thanks|יוֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb for His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
