\q1 \v 14 \rb May the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲ֭בֹתָיו\rb* \rb be remembered|יִזָּכֵ֤ר׀\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and the sin|וְחַטַּ֥את\rb* \rb of his mother|אִ֝מּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb never|אַל־\rb* \rb be blotted out.|תִּמָּֽח׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb May their sins always|תָּמִ֑יד\rb* \rb remain|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb before|נֶֽגֶד־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb that He may cut off|וְיַכְרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb their memory|זִכְרָֽם׃\rb* \rb from the earth.|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb For|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר׀\rb* \rb he never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb thought|זָכַר֮\rb* \rb to show|עֲשׂ֪וֹת\rb* \rb kindness,|חָ֥סֶד\rb*
\q2 \rb but pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֡ף\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb and needy|וְ֭אֶבְיוֹן\rb* \rb and|וְנִכְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb brokenhearted,|לֵבָ֬ב\rb*
\q2 \rb even to their death.|לְמוֹתֵֽת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb The cursing that|קְ֭לָלָה\rb* \rb he loved,|וַיֶּאֱהַ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb may it fall on him;|וַתְּבוֹאֵ֑הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb the blessing|בִּ֝בְרָכָ֗ה\rb* \rb in which he refused|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb to delight,|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb*
\q2 \rb may it be far|וַתִּרְחַ֥ק\rb* \rb from him.|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb The cursing that|קְלָלָ֗ה\rb* \rb he wore|וַיִּלְבַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb like a coat,|כְּמַ֫דּ֥וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb may it soak into|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb his body|בְּקִרְבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb like water,|כַמַּ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and into his bones|בְּעַצְמוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb like oil.|וְ֝כַשֶּׁ֗מֶן\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb May it be|תְּהִי־\rb* \rb like a robe|כְּבֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb wrapped about him,|יַעְטֶ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb like a belt|וּ֝לְמֵ֗זַח\rb* \rb tied|יַחְגְּרֶֽהָ׃\rb* \rb forever around him.|תָּמִ֥יד\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb May this|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb be the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb reward|פְּעֻלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb to my accusers,|שֹׂ֭טְנַי\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb to those who speak|וְהַדֹּבְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb evil|רָ֝֗ע\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb me.|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb But You,|וְאַתָּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb O GOD,|יְה֘וִ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb deal|עֲ‍ֽשֵׂה־\rb* \rb kindly with me|אִ֭תִּי\rb* \rb for the sake of|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb Your name;|שְׁמֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb deliver me|הַצִּילֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb by|כִּי־\rb* \rb the goodness|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb of Your loving devotion.|חַ֝סְדְּךָ֗\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb am poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb and needy;|וְאֶבְי֣וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb my heart|וְ֝לִבִּ֗י\rb* \rb is wounded|חָלַ֥ל\rb* \rb within me.|בְּקִרְבִּֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 23 \rb I am fading away|נֶהֱלָ֑כְתִּי\rb* \rb like a lengthening|כִּנְטוֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb shadow;|כְּצֵל־\rb*
\q2 \rb I am shaken off|נִ֝נְעַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb like a locust.|כָּֽאַרְבֶּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 24 \rb My knees|בִּ֭רְכַּי\rb* \rb are weak|כָּשְׁל֣וּ\rb* \rb from fasting,|מִצּ֑וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb and my body|וּ֝בְשָׂרִ֗י\rb* \rb grows lean|כָּחַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and gaunt.|מִשָּֽׁמֶן׃\rb*
\q1 \v 25 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֤י׀\rb* \rb am|הָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb an object of scorn|חֶרְפָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to my accusers;|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb when they see me,|יִ֝רְא֗וּנִי\rb* \rb they shake|יְנִיע֥וּן\rb* \rb their heads.|רֹאשָֽׁם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb Help me,|עָ֭זְרֵנִי\rb* \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God;|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb save me|ה֭וֹשִׁיעֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb according to Your loving devotion.|כְחַסְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 27 \rb Let them know|וְֽ֭יֵדְעוּ\rb* \rb that this|כִּי־\rb* \rb is Your hand,|יָ֣דְךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|זֹּ֑את\rb* \rb You,|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb have done it.|עֲשִׂיתָֽהּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 28 \rb Though they|הֵמָּה֮\rb* \rb curse,|יְקַֽלְלוּ־\rb* \rb You|וְאַתָּ֪ה\rb* \rb will bless.|תְבָ֫רֵ֥ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb When they rise up,|קָ֤מוּ׀\rb* \rb they will be put to shame,|וַיֵּבֹ֗שׁוּ\rb*
