\q1 \v 29 \rb May my accusers|שׂוֹטְנַ֣י\rb* \rb be clothed|יִלְבְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb with disgrace;|כְּלִמָּ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb may they wear|וְיַעֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb their shame|בָּשְׁתָּֽם׃\rb* \rb like a robe.|כַמְעִ֣יל\rb*
\q1 \v 30 \rb With my mouth|בְּפִ֑י\rb* \rb I will thank|א֘וֹדֶ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb profusely;|מְאֹ֣ד\rb*
\q2 \rb I will praise Him|אֲהַֽלְלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb in the presence|וּבְת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of many.|רַבִּ֣ים\rb*
\q1 \v 31 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He stands|יַ֭עֲמֹד\rb* \rb at the right hand|לִימִ֣ין\rb* \rb of the needy one,|אֶבְי֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb to save him|לְ֝הוֹשִׁ֗יעַ\rb* \rb from the condemners|מִשֹּׁפְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his soul.|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*
\c 110
\s1 God’s Faithful Messiah
\r \ref Genesis 14:17–24|GEN 14:17-24\ref*; \ref Hebrews 5:1–10|HEB 5:1-10\ref*)
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm|מִ֫זְמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of David.|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb*
\q1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb* \rb said|נְאֻ֤ם\rb* \rb to my Lord:|לַֽאדֹנִ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb “Sit|שֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb at My right hand|לִֽימִינִ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I make|אָשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb Your enemies|אֹ֝יְבֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb a footstool|הֲדֹ֣ם\rb* \rb for Your feet.”|לְרַגְלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 110:1 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 22:44|MAT 22:44\ref*, Mark 12:36, Luke 20:42–43, Acts 2:34–35, and Hebrews 1:13\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb extends|יִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb Your mighty|עֻזְּךָ֗\rb* \rb scepter|מַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb from Zion:|מִצִּיּ֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb “Rule|רְ֝דֵ֗ה\rb* \rb in the midst|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb of Your enemies.”|אֹיְבֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֣\rb* \rb shall be willing|נְדָבֹת֮\rb*
\q2 \rb on Your day|בְּי֪וֹם\rb* \rb of battle.|חֵ֫ילֶ֥ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Arrayed in holy|קֹ֭דֶשׁ\rb* \rb splendor,|בְּֽהַדְרֵי־\rb* \rb from the womb|מֵרֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of the dawn,|מִשְׁחָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb to You belongs|לְ֝ךָ֗\rb* \rb the dew|טַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Your youth.|יַלְדֻתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb* \rb has sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb*
\q2 \rb and will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb change His mind:|יִנָּחֵ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \rb “You|אַתָּֽה־\rb* \rb are a priest|כֹהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the order|דִּ֝בְרָתִ֗י\rb*\rb |מַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb of Melchizedek.”|צֶֽדֶק׃\rb*\f + \fr 110:4 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 5:6|HEB 5:6\ref*, Hebrews 7:17, and Hebrews 7:21\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb is at|עַל־\rb* \rb Your right hand;|יְמִֽינְךָ֑\rb*
\q2 \rb He will crush|מָחַ֖ץ\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִֽים׃\rb* \rb in the day|בְּיוֹם־\rb* \rb of His wrath.|אַפּ֣וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb He will judge|יָדִ֣ין\rb* \rb the nations,|בַּ֭גּוֹיִם\rb* \rb heaping up|מָלֵ֣א\rb* \rb the dead;|גְוִיּ֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb He will crush|מָ֥חַץ\rb* \rb the leaders|רֹ֝֗אשׁ\rb* \rb far|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb and wide.|רַבָּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb He will drink|יִשְׁתֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb from the brook|מִ֭נַּחַל\rb* \rb by the road;|בַּדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֝֗ן\rb* \rb He will lift up|יָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb His head.|רֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*
\c 111
\s1 Majestic Is His Work
\q1 \v 1 \rb Hallelujah!|הַ֥לְלוּ\rb*\f + \fr 111:1 \ft Or \fqa Hallelu YAH\ft , meaning \fqa Praise the LORD\ft . This psalm is an acrostic poem, each line beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*\rb |יָ֨הּ׀\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb I will give thanks|אוֹדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb my heart|לֵבָ֑ב\rb*
\q2 \rb in the council|בְּס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the upright|יְשָׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and in the assembly.|וְעֵדָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Great|גְּ֭דֹלִים\rb* \rb are the works|מַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb they are pondered|דְּ֝רוּשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb by all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who delight in them.|חֶפְצֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Splendid|הוֹד־\rb* \rb and majestic|וְהָדָ֥ר\rb* \rb is His work;|פָּֽעֳל֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb His righteousness|וְ֝צִדְקָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb endures|עֹמֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb forever.|לָעַֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb He has caused|עָ֭שָׂה\rb* \rb His wonders|לְנִפְלְאֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb to be remembered;|זֵ֣כֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb is gracious|חַנּ֖וּן\rb* \rb and compassionate.|וְרַח֣וּם\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb He provides|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb food|טֶ֭רֶף\rb* \rb for those who fear Him;|לִֽירֵאָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb He remembers|יִזְכֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb He has shown|הִגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb His people|לְעַמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb the power|כֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb of His works|מַ֭עֲשָׂיו\rb*
\q2 \rb by giving|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָ֝הֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the nations.|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb The works|מַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of His hands|יָ֭דָיו\rb* \rb are truth|אֱמֶ֣ת\rb* \rb and justice;|וּמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His precepts|פִּקּוּדָֽיו׃\rb* \rb are trustworthy.|נֶ֝אֱמָנִ֗ים\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb They are upheld|סְמוּכִ֣ים\rb* \rb forever|לָעַ֣ד\rb* \rb and ever,|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb enacted|עֲ֝שׂוּיִ֗ם\rb* \rb in truth|בֶּאֱמֶ֥ת\rb* \rb and uprightness.|וְיָשָֽׁר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb He has sent|שָׁ֘לַ֤ח\rb* \rb redemption|פְּד֤וּת׀\rb* \rb to His people;|לְעַמּ֗וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He has ordained|צִוָּֽה־\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֑וֹ\rb* \rb forever;|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and awesome|וְנוֹרָ֣א\rb* \rb is His name.|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb The fear|יִרְאַ֬ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb is the beginning|רֵ֘אשִׁ֤ית\rb* \rb of wisdom;|חָכְמָ֨ה׀\rb*
\q2 \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who follow His precepts|עֹשֵׂיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb gain rich|ט֭וֹב\rb* \rb understanding.|שֵׂ֣כֶל\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb His praise|תְּ֝הִלָּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb endures|עֹמֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb forever!|לָעַֽד׃\rb*
\c 112
\s1 The Blessed Fear of the LORD
\r \ref Psalm 128:1–6|PSA 128:1-6\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Hallelujah!|הַ֥לְלוּ\rb*\f + \fr 112:1 \ft Or \fqa Hallelu YAH\ft , meaning \fqa Praise the LORD\ft . This psalm is an acrostic poem, each line beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*\rb |יָ֨הּ׀\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Blessed|אַשְׁרֵי־\rb* \rb is the man|אִ֭ישׁ\rb* \rb who fears|יָרֵ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb who greatly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb delights|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb in His commandments.|בְּ֝מִצְוֺתָ֗יו\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb His descendants|זַרְע֑וֹ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb mighty|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb in the land;|בָּ֭אָרֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb the generation|דּ֭וֹר\rb* \rb of the upright|יְשָׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be blessed.|יְבֹרָֽךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Wealth|הוֹן־\rb* \rb and riches|וָעֹ֥שֶׁר\rb* \rb are in his house,|בְּבֵית֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and his righteousness|וְ֝צִדְקָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb endures|עֹמֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb forever.|לָעַֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Light|א֭וֹר\rb* \rb dawns|זָ֘רַ֤ח\rb* \rb in the darkness|בַּחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb for the upright—|לַיְשָׁרִ֑ים\rb*
