\q2 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb my prayer is ever against|וּ֝תְפִלָּתִ֗י\rb*\rb |ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb the deeds of the wicked.|בְּרָעוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb When their rulers|שֹׁפְטֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb are thrown down|נִשְׁמְט֣וּ\rb* \rb from|בִֽידֵי־\rb* \rb the cliffs,|סֶ֭לַע\rb*
\q2 \rb the people will listen|וְשָׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb to my words,|אֲ֝מָרַ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they are pleasant.|נָעֵֽמוּ׃\rb*
