\d \v 1 \rb A Maskil|מַשְׂכִּ֥יל\rb*\f + \fr 142:1 \fqa Maskil\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for \ref Psalms 32|32\ref*, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.\f* \rb of David,|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb when he was|בִּהְיוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the cave.|בַמְּעָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb A prayer.|תְפִלָּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \rb I cry|אֶזְעָ֑ק\rb* \rb aloud|ק֭וֹלִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I lift my voice|ק֝וֹלִ֗י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb for mercy.|אֶתְחַנָּֽן׃\rb*
