\q2 \rb blessed|אַֽשְׁרֵ֥י\rb* \rb are the people|הָ֝עָ֗ם\rb* \rb whose God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb* \rb is the LORD.|שֶׁיֲהוָ֥ה\rb*
\c 145
\s1 I Will Exalt You, My God and King
\d \v 1 \rb A Psalm of praise.|תְּהִלָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Of David.|לְדָ֫וִ֥ד\rb*\f + \fr 145:1 \ft This psalm is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*
\q1 \rb I will exalt You,|אֲרוֹמִמְךָ֣\rb* \rb my God|אֱלוֹהַ֣י\rb* \rb and King;|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I will bless|וַאֲבָרֲכָ֥ה\rb* \rb Your name|שִׁ֝מְךָ֗\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever.|וָעֶֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb I will bless You,|אֲבָרֲכֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and I will praise|וַאֲהַלְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb Your name|שִׁ֝מְךָ֗\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever.|וָעֶֽד׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Great|גָּ֘ד֤וֹל\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and greatly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb to be praised;|וּמְהֻלָּ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb His greatness|וְ֝לִגְדֻלָּת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb is unsearchable.|חֵֽקֶר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb One generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb will commend|יְשַׁבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Your works|מַעֲשֶׂ֑יךָ\rb* \rb to the next,|לְ֭דוֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb and will proclaim|יַגִּֽידוּ׃\rb* \rb Your mighty acts—|וּגְב֖וּרֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb the glorious|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb splendor|הֲ֭דַר\rb* \rb of Your majesty.|הוֹדֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb And I will meditate|אָשִֽׂיחָה׃\rb* \rb on Your wondrous|נִפְלְאוֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb works.|וְדִבְרֵ֖י\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb They will proclaim|יֹאמֵ֑רוּ\rb* \rb the power|וֶעֱז֣וּז\rb* \rb of Your awesome deeds,|נוֹרְאֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and I will declare|אֲסַפְּרֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb Your greatness.|וּגְדוּלֹּתֶיךָ\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb They will extol|יַבִּ֑יעוּ\rb* \rb the fame|זֵ֣כֶר\rb* \rb of Your abundant|רַב־\rb* \rb goodness|טוּבְךָ֣\rb*
\q2 \rb and sing joyfully of|יְרַנֵּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb Your righteousness.|וְצִדְקָתְךָ֥\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is gracious|חַנּ֣וּן\rb* \rb and compassionate,|וְרַח֣וּם\rb*
\q2 \rb slow|אֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to anger|אַ֝פַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb and abounding|וּגְדָל־\rb* \rb in loving devotion.|חָֽסֶד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb is good|טוֹב־\rb* \rb to all;|לַכֹּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb His compassion|וְ֝רַחֲמָ֗יו\rb* \rb rests on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb He has made.|מַעֲשָֽׂיו׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb You have made|מַעֲשֶׂ֑יךָ\rb* \rb will give You thanks,|יוֹד֣וּךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְ֭הוָה\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your saints|וַ֝חֲסִידֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb will bless You.|יְבָרֲכֽוּכָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb They will tell|יֹאמֵ֑רוּ\rb* \rb of the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of Your kingdom|מַלְכוּתְךָ֣\rb*
\q2 \rb and speak of|יְדַבֵּֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb Your might,|וּגְבוּרָתְךָ֥\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb to make known|לְהוֹדִ֤יעַ׀\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to men|הָ֭אָדָם\rb* \rb Your mighty acts|גְּבוּרֹתָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and the glorious|וּ֝כְב֗וֹד\rb* \rb splendor|הֲדַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Your kingdom.|מַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Your kingdom|מַֽלְכוּתְךָ֗\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb is an everlasting|עֹֽלָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb kingdom,|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your dominion|וּ֝מֶֽמְשֶׁלְתְּךָ֗\rb* \rb endures through all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb generations.|דּ֥וֹר\rb*
\q1 \rb The LORD is faithful in all His words|וָדֽוֹר׃\rb*
\q2 \rb and kind in all His actions.|וָדֽוֹר׃\rb*\f + \fr 145:13 \ft The final two lines are supplied by one MT manuscript, LXX, Syriac, and DSS.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb upholds|סוֹמֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who fall|הַנֹּפְלִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and lifts up|וְ֝זוֹקֵ֗ף\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who are bowed down.|הַכְּפוּפִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb The eyes|עֵֽינֵי־\rb* \rb of all|כֹ֭ל\rb* \rb look|יְשַׂבֵּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb to You,|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and You|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb give|נֽוֹתֵן־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb their food|אָכְלָ֣ם\rb* \rb in season.|בְּעִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb You open|פּוֹתֵ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your hand|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and satisfy|וּמַשְׂבִּ֖יעַ\rb* \rb the desire|רָצֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb of every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb living thing.|חַ֣י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb is righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His ways|דְּרָכָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and kind|וְ֝חָסִ֗יד\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His deeds.|מַעֲשָֽׂיו׃\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb is near|קָר֣וֹב\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who call on Him,|קֹרְאָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb to all|לְכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb call out to Him|יִקְרָאֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb in truth.|בֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb He fulfills|יַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb the desires|רְצוֹן־\rb* \rb of those who fear Him;|יְרֵאָ֥יו\rb*
\q2 \rb He hears|יִ֝שְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb their cry|שַׁוְעָתָ֥ם\rb* \rb and saves them.|וְיוֹשִׁיעֵֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb preserves|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who love Him,|אֹהֲבָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb but|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wicked|הָרְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb He will destroy.|יַשְׁמִֽיד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb My mouth|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb will declare|יְֽדַבֶּ֫ר־\rb* \rb the praise|תְּהִלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb let every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creature|בָּ֭שָׂר\rb* \rb bless|וִיבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb His holy|קָדְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever.|וָעֶֽד׃\rb*
\c 146
\s1 Praise the LORD, O My Soul
\q1 \v 1 \rb Hallelujah!|הַֽלְלוּ־\rb*\f + \fr 146:1 \ft Or \fqa Hallelu YAH\ft , meaning \fqa Praise the LORD\ft ; also in verse 10\f*\rb |יָ֡הּ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Praise|הַלְלִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb O my soul.|נַ֝פְשִׁ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will praise|אֲהַלְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb all my life;|בְּחַיָּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb I will sing praises|אֲזַמְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb to my God|לֵֽאלֹהַ֣י\rb* \rb while I have my being.|בְּעוֹדִֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Put not|אַל־\rb* \rb your trust|תִּבְטְח֥וּ\rb* \rb in princes,|בִנְדִיבִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in mortal|בְּבֶן־\rb* \rb man,|אָדָ֓ם׀\rb* \rb who cannot|שֶׁ֤אֵֽין\rb* \rb save.|תְשׁוּעָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb When his spirit|ר֭וּחוֹ\rb* \rb departs,|תֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb he returns|יָשֻׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to the ground;|לְאַדְמָת֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb on that|הַ֝ה֗וּא\rb* \rb very day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb his plans|עֶשְׁתֹּנֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb perish.|אָבְד֥וּ\rb*
\b 
